{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Professor-%28South-Asian-Studies%29/28760-en_GB": {
      "title": "Professor (South Asian Studies)",
      "description": "Professor (South Asian Studies) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Professor (South Asian Studies) University-Level Unit: Arts & Social Sciences Faculty/Department-Level Unit: South Asian Studies Programme Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 08/10/2026 Job Description The South Asian Studies Programme (SASP), a constituent unit of the Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences, at the National University of Singapore, invites applications for a tenured faculty position, at the Professor (preferably) or Associate Professor rank, in the broad field of South Asian Humanities and Social Sciences, to commence in 2026. The successful candidate will have a strong research agenda focused on South Asia from any of the following fields: History, Sociology, Anthropology, Geography, Environmental Humanities, Political Science, International Relations or Literature, or a combination of these, and must be able to frame teaching and research within the larger connected context of global and inter-Asian history. The candidate must show a proven ability to conduct research in a South Asian language. Further, a credible record of teaching introductory and advanced courses in areas directly related to or very pertinent to South Asia will be advantageous. Upon selection, the candidate will also be expected to assume the position of Head of the South Asian Studies Programme.  A competitive remuneration package, based on qualifications and experience, will be offered to the selected candidate. The South Asian Studies Programme (SASP) is part of the Asian Studies Programme within the Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences. SASP, in which the position will be anchored, was established in 1999 and is multi-disciplinary in its research and teaching (at undergraduate and graduate levels) and has a vibrant community of research students. Application Process Candidates should submit all application materials online via the NUS Careers Portal and addressed to: Chair, Search Committee (Tenured Prof/Assoc Prof Position) South Asian Studies Programme Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences National University of Singapore Other Information Visit our website at http://fass.nus.edu.sg/sas for information on the South Asian Studies Programme. Contact for Further Enquiries Potential candidates are welcome to get in touch with the Chair of the Search Committee to answer any questions they may have at sassec@nus.edu.sg More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: Arts & Social Sciences Department : South Asian Studies Programme Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 28760 Req ID: 28760 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Media-Psychology-and-Emerging-Tech%29/34615-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Media Psychology and Emerging Tech)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Media Psychology and Emerging Tech) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Media Psychology and Emerging Tech) University-Level Unit: Arts & Social Sciences Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Communications And New Media Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 08/10/2026 Job Description The Department of Communications and New Media at the National University of Singapore invites applications for tenure-track positions at the Assistant Professor rank, with expertise in Media Psychology and Emerging Tech . The National University of Singapore (NUS) is a leading research-intensive institution, consistently ranked among the world’s top universities. The University offers a competitive remuneration package, including medical, housing, relocation, and other benefits. Significant research start-up funding is also available Singapore is a modern, English-speaking city-state that serves as a global hub for commerce, finance, and transport. It offers a stable year-round climate and a cosmopolitan mix of cultures and languages. Qualifications PhD in media studies, communication studies, emerging media studies, or a closely related discipline. Application Instructions (Closing Date: 30 October 2026 @ 23:59hrs SGT) A Cover Letter : A cover letter explaining your interest in the position at NUS and the ambition of your research programme, together with a write-up on your top two papers, or the actual publications available. Curriculum Vitae (CV) : A comprehensive CV including a complete list of all post-secondary educational qualifications with dates; employment history since the final degree with dates; complete list of publications and other creative output (separately listing books/monographs, refereed journal articles, and book chapters (distinguishing referred from non-refereed), and research in progress; honours and awards (if applicable): to include major keynote and plenary addresses, invited talks, elected membership in professional and learned societies, membership on editorial board of leading journals; teaching record; university service (if applicable); public and professional service (if applicable). Academic Certificates and Transcripts : Scanned copies of all relevant academic certificates and transcript. Teaching Statement : A statement of teaching philosophy and methodology (maximum 3 pages). Where available, please provide evidence of teaching ability such as student feedback or peer review reports, as well as evidence of other contributions to education (e.g., curriculum development, pedagogical innovation, production of teaching materials). Research Statement : A statement (maximum 3 pages) of major accomplishments in research, citing up to five significant publications, creative work or other scholarly contribution, and explaining their significance. Sample copies of these contributions should be provided (in the case of books, reviews should be provided). A research plan (3-page) with a proposed start-up research budget and utilisation plan for the next 3-5 years. External Reference Letters : Candidates should arrange for at least three referees, including the PhD advisor, to send letters of reference directly to the department / faculty. The references need to include both the PhD advisor and Postdoctoral supervisor as applicable. Referees should benchmark your research performance against peers at equivalent and top institutions or programmes and must send their letters directly to cnmcareer@nus.edu.sg. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. For any questions, please email cnmcareer@nus.edu.sg. Req ID: 34615 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Associate-Professor-%28Composition-and-Creative-Practice%29/34518-en_GB": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Composition and Creative Practice)",
      "description": "Associate Professor (Composition and Creative Practice) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Associate Professor (Composition and Creative Practice) University-Level Unit: Yong Siew Toh Conservatory of Music Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office (YST Conservatory of Music) Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 28/09/2026 Job Description The Yong Siew Toh Conservatory, National University of Singapore, offers a unique and adventurous 21st-century Asian environment in which we train and educate performers, composers, producers and recording engineers to take advantage of future professional and artistic opportunities both in Singapore and in the world. The Conservatory is distinctively international in terms of its faculty, student population and artistic outlook. Our mission is to be a focal point for musical activity, artistic development and research, for Singapore, the Asia-Pacific region, and beyond. YST is seeking an experienced music professional to provide strategic academic and artistic leadership in composition, creative practice, and artistic research. The successful candidate will advance an imaginative and integrated model of conservatory education at NUS that connects creative practice, scholarly inquiry, teaching, and curriculum development in composition, aural training, music theory, and contextual studies with professional development, leadership, and public engagement. Through internationally recognised creative practice, artistic research, and regional and international engagement, the candidate will also contribute to the Conservatory’s position as a leading centre for contemporary and creative practice in music and for artistic research, with particular distinction in Southeast Asia and strong international connections. Key responsibilities: Provide academic, artistic, and strategic leadership in the development of Composition and Creative Practice as an integrated area, contributing to creative practice, artistic research, teaching, curriculum development, and the strategic development of the Conservatory and the wider University arts sector Advance an internationally recognised programme of creative practice through composition, artistic research, performances, recordings, publications, and collaborations with performers, ensembles, festivals, universities, and cultural institutions. Design, teach and develop undergraduate and postgraduate courses in composition, music theory, artistic research, creativity, interdisciplinary practice, and related areas, integrating creative practice, analytical inquiry, performance, and professional preparation Develop pedagogical approaches that connect theoretical understanding with creative and artistic practice, reflective inquiry, and interdisciplinary learning, fostering student-centred and practice-led education Provide strategic leadership in curriculum development, programme review and integration of creative practice, artistic research, interdisciplinary learning, and conservatory education Supervise and mentor undergraduate, postgraduate, professional, and lifelong learners, fostering artistic distinction, critical inquiry, creativity, and professional development through inclusive and practice-led learning environments Provide strategic leadership in the development of regional and international artistic partnerships, with strengthening connections between Southeast Asia and the international contemporary music community through collaborations with composers, performers, ensembles, festivals, universities, cultural organisations and networks Provide artistic and academic leadership in advancing contemporary music, creative practice, and artistic research in Southeast Asia through composition, commissions, collaborations, the curation of concerts, festivals, conferences, and public engagement initiatives, alongside activity and professional service that strengthen Southeast Asia's contemporary music ecosystem and enhance its international profile and impact Maintain an active and internationally recognised programme of creative practice and artistic research that informs teaching, curriculum development, strategic leadership, and the advancement of the discipline Qualifications The selection process will commence in November 2026.  Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted.  Enquiries about the position may be directed to the Dean’s Office at mussec@nus.edu.sg. Requirements for interested applicants include: A doctoral degree in Composition, Artistic Research, or a related field of musical practice. A minimum of ten years of successful teaching experience in a conservatory and/or university environment, with a sustained record of impactful teaching, curriculum design and development, academic leadership, and student mentorship across undergraduate and postgraduate education. An internationally recognised profile as a composer-scholar or creative practitioner, demonstrated through a substantial body of creative work, artistic research outputs, publications, commissions, performances, recordings, and collaborations. Demonstrated expertise and leadership in integrating composition, creative practice, artistic research, music theory, interdisciplinary teaching, and curriculum design and development within a conservatory or university environment. Proven experience in academic and institutional leadership, curriculum design and development, programme review, and institutional service, with the ability to provide strategic leadership in higher institution educational development and conservatory advancement. A sustained record in supervising and mentoring students, emerging artists, and professionals across undergraduate, postgraduate, and lifelong learning contexts. Demonstrated artistic and professional leadership in developing regional and international networks, partnerships, and collaborative initiatives that advance contemporary music, artistic research, and creative practice, with particular distinction in strengthening Southeast Asia's engagement within the international music community. Excellent communication, organisational, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and provide strategic academic leadership within a dynamic university and conservatory environment. Evidence of continuing artistic distinction, scholarly achievement, strategic leadership, and international standing. Rank / Salary: Tenure-track at the rank of Associate Professor with benefits package commensurate with qualifications and experience in line with NUS appointment norms. Qualified candidates should submit the following materials to the Search Committee via the NUS recruitment portal ( https://www.nus.edu.sg/careers/) : A letter of interest describing your vision and your relevant experiences. A current curriculum vitae outlining professional, teaching, and administrative experience. Three letters of recommendation from professional referees. A detailed portfolio or documentation of representative composition and creative practice projects, programmes, or initiatives you have led or coordinated. Links to recordings, productions, or other artistic work where relevant. Req ID: 34518 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Department-of-Anatomy%29/34503-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Department of Anatomy)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Department of Anatomy) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Department of Anatomy) University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Anatomy Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 25/09/2026 The National University of Singapore is one of the top universities worldwide. We invite applications from outstanding scholars for tenure-track positions at the rank of Assistant Professor or higher in the Department of Anatomy, Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine. Applicants should hold a PhD/MBBS/MD degree with post-doctoral research experience Evidence of excellence in research. The department currently run research programmes in neuroscience and cancer Successful candidates are expected to participate in the department teaching programmes in gross anatomy, histology and embryology. The medical school offers competitive full salary, start-up research funding and other allowances including medical and housing benefits (if applicable). Interested candidates should send their CV, research plan, teaching portfolio and at least three reference letters to: Mr Kee Wei Li Assistant Manager Department of Anatomy antsec@nus.edu Applications are reviewed on an ongoing basis. Only short-listed candidates will be notified. Req ID: 34503 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Department-of-Physiology-and-CSI%29/34390-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Department of Physiology and CSI)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Department of Physiology and CSI) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Department of Physiology and CSI) University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Physiology Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 11/09/2026 . Candidates are expected to bring strong expertise in cancer epigenetics, RNA biology, functional genomics, and mechanistic cancer research, and to build a high-impact programme aligned with CSI Singapore’s strategic priorities. Key Responsibilities Research Leadership Establish and lead an independent research programme focused on cancer biology, with emphasis on: cancer epigenetics and chromatin regulation RNA biology and gene regulation tumour state plasticity and lineage programmes functional genomics and mechanistic cancer discovery integration of single-cell, spatial, and multi-omic approaches Scientific Innovation Candidates are expected to drive innovation by developing novel concepts, methods, and experimental approaches that advance understanding of cancer biology. The work should push beyond incremental findings toward discoveries with the potential to reshape current thinking in the field. Grant Development & Research Funding Secure competitive national and international research funding. Lead multi-investigator grant applications and collaborative research initiatives. Manage research budgets and ensure efficient utilisation of research resources. Research Team Leadership Recruit, supervise, and mentor research fellows, research assistants, graduate students, and other laboratory personnel. Foster a collaborative, innovative, and inclusive laboratory culture. Provide scientific mentorship and career development for junior researchers. Collaboration Develop interdisciplinary collaborations across CSI Singapore, NUS, healthcare institutions, and international research organisations. Partner with clinician-scientists to facilitate translational and precision oncology research. Engage with pharmaceutical and biotechnology partners where appropriate to accelerate therapeutic development. Scholarly Activities Publish high-impact scientific findings in leading peer-reviewed journals. Present research findings at international scientific conferences and symposia. Serve on scientific advisory panels, grant review committees, and editorial boards as appropriate. Teaching & Academic Contributions Contribute to graduate education through supervision of postgraduate students. Participate in teaching, seminars, journal clubs, and academic training programmes within NUS. Support institutional initiatives in research excellence and talent development. Laboratory & Compliance Management Ensure compliance with institutional, biosafety, ethical, and regulatory requirements. Oversee laboratory operations, equipment, and research infrastructure. Promote good research practices and research integrity. Skill Set Requirements Essential PhD in a relevant biomedical or life sciences discipline. Strong postdoctoral track record in cancer research or closely related fields. Demonstrated ability to conduct innovative, independent, and rigorous research. First-author and/or senior-author publications in reputable journals. Expertise in one or more of the following: Cancer biology Tumour microenvironment Epigenetics RNA biology Genomics / multi-omics Functional genomics Mechanistic molecular biology Experience with experimental design, data interpretation, and scientific writing. Evidence of grant readiness or prior success in competitive funding applications. Strong leadership, mentorship, and team-building potential. Ability to collaborate across disciplines and communicate effectively. Desirable Experience with translational or clinically relevant cancer research. Familiarity with single-cell or spatial omics, CRISPR screening, or advanced genomic technologies. Experience working in internationally competitive research environments. Clear potential to develop an original, fundable, and high-impact research niche. Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration with clinicians, computational scientists, and industry partners. Req ID: 34390 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Tenure-Track%29/34340-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office (Medicine) Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 07/09/2026 - PI Name: A/Prof Zhang Yong Liang Department/Centre/Programme: Dept of Microbiology and Immunology, associated with Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) Position: Assistant Professor The National University of Singapore invites applications for Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) for <Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP)> in the Department of Microbiology and Immunology, Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine. The Department of Microbiology and Immunology has distinguished itself in biomedical research and has a broad spectrum of expertise. Research in the Department encompasses very diverse questions and uses a wide variety of approaches, experimental systems, and techniques. Principal Investigators of the Department are internationally recognized for research on immunology, medical virology, bacteriology, parasitology, molecular biology and biotechnology. More information on the department is available at https://medicine.nus.edu.sg/pcm/ . Purpose of the post Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) will work closely with the Principal Investigator to develop and lead a research program in Immunology, with a focus on translational research that bridges fundamental discoveries and clinical applications. Main duties and responsibilities The Assistant Professor will be able to: Establish an independent, externally funded research program in immunology with an emphasis on translational approaches. Conduct cutting-edge research that contributes to ITRP’s goals, including vaccine development, antimicrobial resistance, pathogen-host interactions, anti-tumor immunity, immune ageing, and public health interventions. Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams including clinicians, scientists, and other stakeholders to drive impactful research. Mentor and supervise undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral researchers. Teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses in areas related to microbiology or immunology, anchored under the Department of Microbiology & Immunology. Publish high-quality, peer-reviewed research in leading journals and present findings at national and international conferences. Actively participate in ITRP’s events, workshops, and outreach activities. Qualifications The applicant should possess the following: Essential •    PhD, MD, or equivalent, with at least three years of postdoctoral experience in microbiology, immunology, epidemiology, or a related field. •    Proven track record of research excellence as evidenced by first author original high impact publications. •    Strong potential to secure competitive external funding. •    Expertise in translational research methodologies. •    Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary teams. •    Excellent communication and leadership skills. Desirable •    Experience in teaching and curriculum development at the graduate level. •    Experience in mentoring and supervising research trainees. •    Research experience in neutrophil biology, microbial infection, and sepsis. •    Familiarity with regulatory and ethical requirements for translational research. <Note to Administrators/PIs: The criteria above for appointment should follow the policy guidelines on the standard/indices of the appointment e.g. an outstanding educator with a PhD degree and generally 6 or more years’ postdoctoral experience etc.> Remuneration will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 34340 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Tenure%29-in-Architecture-and-Technology/31953-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure) in Architecture and Technology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Tenure) in Architecture and Technology Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Tenure) in Architecture and Technology University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Architecture Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 05/09/2026 Job Description The Department of Architecture invites applications for one Tenure Track position in Architecture and Technology at the rank of Assistant Professor. The Department of Architecture in the College of Design and Engineering is ranked among the top 10 in the world, and Asia’s best in Architecture/Built Environment, by the Quacquarelli Symonds (QS) World University Rankings (2025). It offers the professionally accredited Master of Architecture programme as well as a range of graduate and undergraduate programmes in related fields such as urban planning and design, architectural conservation and landscape architecture. The faculty is correspondingly diverse and international. The Department offers internationally competitive remuneration, generous employment benefits as well as access to research funding for both junior and senior academics. International applicants will also receive subsidised housing at Kent Vale, a faculty residence on the NUS campus. Qualifications The Technologies Cluster at the Department of Architecture seeks highly qualified applicants actively engaged in interdisciplinary research focused on, but not limited to, one or more of the following themes: (1) Architectural materials and construction (2) Computational thinking and parametric modelling The successful candidate is expected to teach one or more core courses, particularly in areas related to the above themes. The candidate should also be interested in running a design studio in an interdisciplinary setting. The candidate is expected to develop an interdisciplinary research agenda adopting and developing advanced technological, computational and/or material approaches to address pressing challenges to the built environment, particularly within Asia. They are strongly encouraged to pursue collaborative research in the context of the College of Design and Engineering as well as with industry partners and government agencies within and beyond Singapore. The candidate should possess a Ph.D. degree in Architecture, Architectural Technology, Engineering or related disciplines, as well as requisite experience and credentials suitable for full-time tenure-track appointments in NUS.  Alternatively, applicants can express their preference for a practice-track position if they can demonstrate strong professional experience in the relevant fields. For these applicants, they should submit a portfolio showing major projects and other forms of practice in addition to other requirements. They should also hold a relevant graduate degree (Master or above) by the time of appointment. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.  To apply, please provide the required documents in pdf and indicate which position you are applying for by 15 May 2026 .  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to deliver a seminar at NUS between August and November 2026. Expected start date of the appointment is early to mid-2027. 1.   A letter of interest 2.   A complete Curriculum Vitae 3.   A statement of Teaching (maximum two pages) and a sample syllabus of a course to be taught that is relevant to the above-mentioned themes. 4.   A statement of Research (including a short research plan for next three to five years maximum three pages) – citing up to five significant publications, creative work or other scholarly contribution and explaining their significance, and a writing sample. 5.    A complete list of publications, grouped according to papers, books, and reviews, including page numbers, in bibliographic form. 6.    Names of four referees with contact details (who will be contacted only if shortlisted).  Please highlight any referee who was a member of your PhD dissertation committee. In accordance with the Personal Data Protection Act (PDPA), please provide consent for the collection, use and disclosure of personal data, using the NUS Personal Data Consent for Job Applicants form. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: College of Design and Engineering Department : Architecture Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 31953 Req ID: 31953 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Tenure%29-in-Architectural-Conservation/31954-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure) in Architectural Conservation",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Tenure) in Architectural Conservation Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Tenure) in Architectural Conservation University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Architecture Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 05/09/2026 Job Description The Department of Architecture invites applications for one Tenure Track position in Architectural Conservation at the rank of Assistant Professor. The Master of Arts in Architectural Conservation programme is a one-year graduate degree that specializes in conservation policy, architectural history, construction and preservation techniques and heritage management. It provides a distinct approach that is sensitive to the cultural richness of the Asian region as well as its urban challenges. Graduates of the programme move on to find careers in historic building conservation, architectural design consulting and other fields in both the public and private sectors. The Department of Architecture in the College of Design and Engineering is ranked among the top 10 in the world, and Asia’s best in Architecture/Built Environment, based on the Quacquarelli Symonds (QS) World University Rankings (2025). It offers the professionally accredited Master of Architecture programme as well as a range of graduate and undergraduate programmes in related fields such as urban planning/design, landscape architecture and conservation. The faculty is correspondingly diverse and international. The Department offers internationally competitive remuneration, generous employment benefits as well as access to research funding for both junior and senior academics. International applicants will also receive subsidized housing at Kent Vale, a faculty residence on the NUS campus. Qualifications We are looking for a highly qualified, interdisciplinary, and inspirational candidate for the position of Assistant Professor in Architectural Conservation (Tenure Track).  He/she should have relevant research expertise in policies, philosophies and practices pertaining to architectural and urban heritage. A strong focus on the Southeast Asian (or Asia more generally) context is essential. Tenure track faculty are expected to develop a compelling research agenda and demonstrate a high level of intellectual engagement with commensurate levels of productivity. They are also strongly encouraged to pursue collaborative research in the context of the College of Design and Engineering as well as with industry partners and government agencies within and beyond Singapore. A PhD is a prerequisite for this position. The Department particularly welcomes applications from candidates whose research and teaching focus on conservation materials and technologies, including but not limited to heritage science, diagnostics and monitoring, digital heritage documentation, material conservation, sustainable conservation interventions, and emerging technologies for the preservation and management of cultural heritage. In addition to research, the successful candidate is expected to teach core, elective and/or studio courses in accordance with the expected teaching load of full-time faculty in the department and his/her areas of specialization. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.  To apply, please provide the required documents in pdf and indicate which position you are applying for by 24 September 2026 .  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to deliver a seminar at NUS between August and December 2026.  Expected start of the appointment is early to mid-2027. 1.   A letter of interest 2.   A complete Curriculum Vitae 3.   A statement of Teaching (maximum two pages) and a sample syllabus of a course to be taught that is relevant to the position advertised. 4.   A statement of Research (including a short research plan for next three to five years maximum three pages) – citing up to five significant publications, creative work or other scholarly contribution and explaining their significance, and a writing sample. 5.    A complete list of publications, grouped according to papers, books, and reviews, including page numbers, in bibliographic form. 6.    A portfolio showing major projects and other forms of professional practice (optional). 7.    Names of four referees with contact details (who will be contacted only if shortlisted).  Please highlight any referee who was a member of your PhD dissertation committee. In accordance with the Personal Data Protection Act (PDPA), please provide consent for the collection, use and disclosure of personal data, using the NUS Personal Data Consent for Job Applicants form. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: College of Design and Engineering Department : Architecture Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 31954 Req ID: 31954 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Associate-Professor-%28Practice%29-in-Architectural-Conservation/32143-en_GB": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Practice) in Architectural Conservation",
      "description": "Associate Professor (Practice) in Architectural Conservation Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Associate Professor (Practice) in Architectural Conservation University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Architecture Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 05/09/2026 Job Description The Department of Architecture invites applications for the position of Programme Director of the Master of Arts in Architectural Conservation programme at the rank of Associate Professor (Practice Track). The Master of Arts in Architectural Conservation programme is a one-year graduate degree that specializes in conservation policy, architectural history, construction and preservation techniques and heritage management. It provides a distinct approach that is sensitive to the cultural richness of the Asian region as well as its urban challenges. Graduates of the programme move on to find careers in historic building conservation, architectural design consulting and other fields in both the public and private sectors. The Department of Architecture in the College of Design and Engineering is ranked among the top 10 in the world, and Asia’s best in Architecture/Built Environment, based on the Quacquarelli Symonds (QS) World University Rankings (2025). It offers the professionally accredited Master of Architecture programme as well as a range of graduate and undergraduate programmes in related fields such as urban planning/design, landscape architecture and conservation. The faculty is correspondingly diverse and international. The Department offers internationally competitive remuneration, generous employment benefits as well as access to research funding for both junior and senior academics. International applicants will also receive subsidized housing at Kent Vale, a faculty residence on the NUS campus. Qualifications We are looking for a senior and highly regarded professional in the field of architectural conservation and heritage management to assume this position. He/she will be a visionary leader with a demonstrated ability to work with a diverse team and build networks in and outside of academia. The duties of the Programme Director include: (1)    Strategic positioning of the programme to build on its reputation and visibility in the international arena; (2)    Managing and overseeing curricular content and manpower needs of the courses; (3)    Attend to the needs of staff and students in the programme; and (4)   Liaising with the Head of Department and the management team to ensure the smooth running of the programme in accordance with the policies of the College and the University. The successful candidate is also expected to teach core, elective and/or studio courses in accordance with the expected teaching load of full-time faculty in the Department and his/her areas of specialization. In general, those applying for the rank of Associate Professor should demonstrate a strong and sustained career in practice for 6 years and above.  A graduate-level architectural degree with accreditations by professional bodies is essential for the position. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.  To apply, please provide the required documents in pdf and indicate which position you are applying for by 15 May 2026 .  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to deliver a seminar at NUS between August and December 2026.  Expected start of the appointment is early to mid-2027. 1.   A letter of interest 2.   A complete Curriculum Vitae 3.   A portfolio showing major projects and other forms of professional practice. This should be accompanied by a statement of professional accomplishments and how they are relevant to the position advertised. 4.   A statement of Teaching (maximum two pages) and a sample syllabus of a course to be taught. 5.   A statement of Research (maximum three pages) and a writing sample. 6.   A complete list of publications, patents, and other inventions and creative activity. 7.   Names of four referees with contact details (who will be contacted only if shortlisted). In accordance with the Personal Data Protection Act (PDPA), please provide consent for the collection, use and disclosure of personal data, using the NUS Personal Data Consent for Job Applicants form. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 32143 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor%2C-AI-Pathogen-Genomics/34211-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, AI Pathogen Genomics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, AI Pathogen Genomics Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor, AI Pathogen Genomics University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office Employee Category: Research Staff Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 02/09/2026 Job Description The Duke-NUS Centre for Outbreak Preparedness (COP) works to strengthen communicable disease preparedness and response capacity across South and Southeast Asia. COP also hosts the Asia Pathogen Genomics Initiative (Asia PGI), a regional network supporting 15 countries to strengthen pathogen genomics surveillance, data use and translation for public health action. The Duke-NUS Centre for Biomedical Data Science (CBDS) provides a strategic hub for data science, artificial intelligence, statistical methodology, computational omics and systems biology, supporting biomedical discovery and translational impact across Duke-NUS, SingHealth, the Academic Medical Centre and wider regional and global partners. This joint appointment will advance research and platform development at the interface of AI and pathogen genomics, bringing together COP’s applied focus on infectious disease threats and regional preparedness with CBDS’s depth in biomedical data science, AI and computational biology. Key responsibilities will include: Lead and develop applied research at the interface of AI, pathogen genomics and outbreak preparedness, in close collaboration with COP and CBDS faculty and partners. Design, develop and evaluate AI-enabled methods for pathogen genomic analysis, including approaches for variant detection, lineage classification, antimicrobial resistance prediction, outbreak clustering, genomic representation learning, multi-modal data integration and decision support. Build collaborations across Duke-NUS, SingHealth, national public health agencies, regional academic partners, ministries of health, international organisations and technology partners. Contribute to grant proposals, research strategy, donor engagement and externally funded programmes in AI, pathogen genomics, infectious disease surveillance and regional health security. Publish high-quality scientific papers, technical reports, policy briefs and other outputs that advance the field and support translation into public health practice. Support robust, reproducible and ethically governed analytical workflows, including attention to data quality, privacy, security, sovereignty, transparency, validation and responsible AI. Provide scientific and technical leadership to research staff, data scientists, students and collaborators, including supervision, mentorship and capacity development. Contribute to education and training in AI, computational genomics, biomedical data science and outbreak analytics for Duke-NUS learners and regional partners. Help translate analytical outputs into practical insights for surveillance, preparedness, outbreak response and policy decision-making. Perform other related duties as required by COP and CBDS leadership. Qualifications Appointment level will be commensurate with qualifications and experience, including evidence of research independence, scientific output, leadership, grant development, teaching or mentorship, and ability to work across academic, public health and technical teams. Minimum qualifications include: PhD or equivalent doctoral qualification in artificial intelligence, machine learning, computational biology, bioinformatics, genomics, infectious disease modelling, biomedical data science, statistics, computer science or a closely related field. Minimum experience commensurate with appointment: Senior Research Fellow - normally at least 5 years of postdoctoral or equivalent research experience; Principal Research Scientist - normally at least 6 years of relevant experience with evidence of research independence and leadership; Assistant Professor (Practice Track) - substantial applied research/practice experience with evidence of teaching, mentorship or capacity development. Demonstrated expertise in AI/data science methods applied to genomics, omics, infectious diseases, public health surveillance or related biomedical domains. Strong technical skills in areas such as machine learning, statistical learning, scalable analytical pipelines, software engineering, cloud or high-performance computing, federated or privacy-preserving analytics, knowledge graphs, LLMs or multi-modal data integration. Track record of high-quality research outputs, technical delivery, grant/proposal development, team science and effective communication with academic, public health and technical stakeholders. The ideal candidate will combine scientific credibility with practical implementation experience. They should be comfortable working across disciplines, from machine learning and genomics to public health and policy, and motivated to build AI-enabled genomic intelligence approaches that are rigorous, responsible and useful for real-world outbreak preparedness in Asia and beyond. Req ID: 34211 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28VAC%29/30075-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (VAC)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (VAC) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (VAC) University-Level Unit: Arts & Social Sciences Faculty/Department-Level Unit: English, Linguistics and Theatre Studies Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 02/09/2026 Job Description The National University of Singapore invites exceptional candidates to apply for a tenure-track Assistant Professor or Associate Professor position in Visual Arts and Cultures. Scholars of all research specializations relevant to the field are encouraged to apply. Priority will be given to candidates who can expand our current portfolio of teaching and research expertise (see our faculty profiles here). Programme Information The Art History Minor at NUS is one of the top-ranked programmes in the field internationally and is housed in the Department of History, Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences (FASS). The Minor and its sister Visual Cultures Minor (Department of Communications and New Media) are aligned with a Visual Arts and Cultures Second Major (Department of English, Linguistics and Theatre Studies) forming a unique interdisciplinary pathway. The programmes work in close partnership with the National Gallery Singapore, NUS Museum and other leading exhibiting institutions, exposing students to both discursive agendas and practical realities in the sector. Aligned with NUS’s mission to educate and transform, and our commitment to cultivating a vibrant community of students with creative and critical capacities, FASS VAC invites applications for Assistant/Associate Professorship in Visual Arts and Cultures, a full-time tenure-track faculty position in the Department of English, Linguistics and Theatre Studies. Enquiries may be directed to ellsec@nus.edu.sg. Further information about working at the National University of Singapore is available at https://www.nus.edu.sg/careers . The Department website can be found at https://fass.nus.edu.sg/elts/ . Qualifications Applicants must hold a PhD or equivalent qualification in the visual art, visual culture or a cognate field at the point of application.  We seek scholars with strong publication records in leading journals and university presses who are also accomplished educators capable of teaching across multiple levels - from introductory courses for non-majors to graduate seminars - and who can develop interdisciplinary connections within the arts and humanities. For the Visual Arts and Cultures role, we especially welcome applicants whose expertise spans more than one of the following areas: history and theory of modern and  contemporary art, architecture, design, or visual/material culture; visual studies (including visual anthropology); literary and cultural studies; cultural theory and criticism; exhibition studies; and curatorial studies. Applicants whose research includes practice-based or creative methodologies are also encouraged to apply, particularly where these intersect with scholarly inquiry in those fields. While we do not require a regional specialization, candidates with research expertise or professional experience in Southeast Asian art, visual culture or exhibitions will be favourably considered. Salaries are internationally competitive, with benefits including subsidized housing. FASS tenure-track professors typically teach 3 courses a year. Application materials Applicants should submit the following documents: A cover letter addressing: How the candidate's expertise will expand our current research and teaching portfolio. Evidence of research excellence, including publication record and research trajectory. Evidence of teaching excellence, including experience across different course levels. A complete CV Research and teaching statements Two signature publications by the applicant as lead author Contact information of three referees. If the applicant is two or more years post-PhD, the reviewers should not be limited to supervisors. For shortlisted applicants, the Search Committee will contact the referees directly for their reviews. The referees will be asked to compare the applicant’s research performance to specific individuals at equivalent and top institutions and/or programs. For full consideration, please submit a complete application package (with all the above documents) at by 2 October 2026. Applications received after this date may still be considered until the position is filled. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: Arts & Social Sciences Department : English, Linguistics and Theatre Studies Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 30075 Req ID: 30075 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor/34290-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Biochemistry Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 02/09/2026 . Candidates are expected to bring strong expertise in cancer mechanisms, genomics, epigenetics, or RNA biology, and to develop a high-impact programme aligned with CSI Singapore’s strategic priorities. Key Responsibilities Research Leadership Establish and lead an independent research programme investigating cancer biology, including cancer epigenetics and chromatin regulation RNA biology and gene regulation tumour state plasticity and lineage programmes functional genomics and mechanistic cancer discovery integration of single-cell, spatial, and multi-omic approaches Translate fundamental discoveries into clinically relevant applications, including  therapeutics, biomarkers, and drug development. Scientific Innovation Candidates are expected to drive innovation by developing novel concepts, methods, and experimental approaches that advance understanding of cancer biology. The work should push beyond incremental findings toward discoveries with the potential to reshape current thinking in the field. Grant Development & Research Funding Secure competitive national and international research funding. Lead multi-investigator grant applications and collaborative research initiatives. Manage research budgets and ensure efficient utilisation of research resources. Research Team Leadership Recruit, supervise, and mentor research fellows, research assistants, graduate students, and other laboratory personnel. Foster a collaborative, innovative, and inclusive laboratory culture. Provide scientific mentorship and career development for junior researchers. Collaboration Develop interdisciplinary collaborations across CSI Singapore, NUS, healthcare institutions, and international research organisations. Partner with clinician-scientists to facilitate translational and precision oncology research. Engage with pharmaceutical and biotechnology partners where appropriate to accelerate therapeutic development. Scholarly Activities Publish high-impact scientific findings in leading peer-reviewed journals. Present research findings at international scientific conferences and symposia. Serve on scientific advisory panels, grant review committees, and editorial boards as appropriate. Teaching & Academic Contributions Contribute to graduate education through supervision of postgraduate students. Participate in teaching, seminars, journal clubs, and academic training programmes within NUS. Support institutional initiatives in research excellence and talent development. Laboratory & Compliance Management Ensure compliance with institutional, biosafety, ethical, and regulatory requirements. Oversee laboratory operations, equipment, and research infrastructure. Promote good research practices and research integrity. Skill Set Requirements Essential PhD in a relevant biomedical or life sciences discipline. Strong postdoctoral track record in cancer research or closely related fields. Demonstrated ability to conduct innovative, independent, and rigorous research. First-author and/or senior-author publications in reputable journals. Expertise in one or more of the following: Cancer biology Tumour microenvironment Epigenetics RNA biology Genomics / multi-omics Functional genomics Mechanistic molecular biology Experience with experimental design, data interpretation, and scientific writing. Evidence of grant readiness or prior success in competitive funding applications. Strong leadership, mentorship, and team-building potential. Ability to collaborate across disciplines and communicate effectively. Desirable Experience with translational or clinically relevant cancer research. Familiarity with single-cell or spatial omics, CRISPR screening, or advanced genomic technologies. Experience working in internationally competitive research environments. Clear potential to develop an original, fundable, and high-impact research niche. Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration with clinicians, computational scientists, and industry partners. Req ID: 34290 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor/34266-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean-Med-Human Potential Translational Research Programme Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 31/08/2026 Assistant Professor at the Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine, National University of Singapore The Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine at the National University of Singapore invites applications for a faculty position in Heat Resilience & Performance Centre (HRPC) and Human Potential Translational Research Programme (HP TRP). We seek outstanding candidates who will develop an independent and internationally competitive research programme that advances understanding of physiological processes in health and disease. About the Role The successful candidate will establish and lead research that complements existing strengths within the School of Medicine and contributes to interdisciplinary research, education, and translational impact. Areas of interest may include, but are not limited to: Environmental, exercise, occupational, or performance physiology Data-driven, computational, or technology-enabled physiology research Key Responsibilities The appointee will be expected to: Develop and sustain an independent research programme in physiology Conduct high-quality basic, translational, clinical, or applied research Publish in reputable peer-reviewed journals Secure competitive research funding Build collaborations within NUS and with external partners Mentor students, research staff, and early-career researchers Contribute to undergraduate and/or graduate education where appropriate Support the School’s academic, research, and service activities Translate research findings into scientific, clinical, public health, or policy-relevant outcomes where applicable Qualifications Applicants should have: A PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent degree in Physiology, Biomedical Science, Medicine, Life Sciences, or a related discipline Relevant postdoctoral, clinical, or independent research experience A strong publication record appropriate to career stage Strong analytical, experimental, quantitative, computational, or translational research skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary environment Commitment to mentoring, academic development, and research excellence Preferred Experience Experience in one or more of the following areas would be advantageous: Physiology research in health and disease Translational or interdisciplinary biomedical research Human participant, animal, cellular, molecular, or computational studies Collaboration across clinical, engineering, public health, or life science disciplines Concise version: The Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine, National University of Singapore, invites applications for a Tenure Track faculty position. Appointment will primarily be at the Assistant Professor level. We seek outstanding candidates who will establish an independent, internationally competitive research programme that advances understanding of physiological processes in health and disease. Research areas may include, but are not limited to, environmental, exercise, occupational, or performance physiology; and data-driven or technology-enabled approaches to physiological research. The successful candidate will be expected to conduct high-quality research, publish in leading peer-reviewed journals, secure competitive funding, build local and international collaborations, mentor students and research staff, and contribute to teaching and academic service where appropriate. Applicants should have a PhD, MD/PhD or equivalent degree in Physiology, Biomedical Science, Medicine, Life Sciences or a related discipline. Candidates should demonstrate a strong publication record, research leadership potential, ability to attract external funding, and commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and mentoring. Req ID: 34266 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Professor-%28HSRPH-MO%29/31872-en_GB": {
      "title": "Professor (HSRPH/ MO)",
      "description": "Professor (HSRPH/ MO) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Professor (HSRPH/ MO) University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Office of Research Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 27/08/2026 Job Description The Signature Research Programme in Health Services Research and Population Health (“HSRPH”) in Duke-NUS Medical School is a centre of academic excellence for research and education on Population Health and the organisation, funding and delivery of health services. The programme’s focus is on population health and clinical service innovation in an increasingly complex and connected world. The major research focus of HSRPH is the organisation and delivery of health and social services in the context of an ageing population. We are also developing a range of education activities for healthcare professionals including short courses, graduate certificates, Master’s courses and PhD programmes. We invite applications for a tenure-track/tenured faculty position based in Singapore at the rank of Associate Professor/ Professor. Job title, salaries and benefits will be commensurate with the candidate’s accomplishments and experiences. Job Responsibilities: We are seeking a researcher whose research methods might include quantitative and qualitative research, behavioural, decision and implementation science. Focus areas might include mental health, ageing, environment and health, population health, healthcare finance and health policy  with the aim to inform clinical and public policy decision making; and is able to lead and publish research that moves the discipline forward. The ideal candidate will enjoy a multidisciplinary environment and will establish an innovative, pragmatic, world leading research agenda. He/She will provide consultancy services, build capacity by mentoring clinicians and other researchers and supporting relevant education activities. Opportunities exist for productive collaborations with world-class researchers within HSRPH and with SingHealth clinicians and other staff and other national health care organizations, as well as the SingHealth Duke-NUS Global Health Institute. This tenure-track/tenured position represents an outstanding opportunity for an established investigator. Qualifications Requirements & Responsibilities: •    Bring together and develop a team of researchers. •    Create a distinctive research programme. •    Track record of applied research and methods-based publications. •    Track record of independent research and collaboration with clinical and policy partners. •    Track record in securing research grants. Other Skills and Personal Attributes Required: •    A relevant PhD or equivalent qualification •    Leadership skills •    An ability to work collaboratively. •    Existing mentoring skills or willingness to develop these •    Ability to work with applied projects and methodology •    Skills in communicating complex ideas to non-technical audiences We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 31872 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Lecturer-%28Data-Literacy%29/34151-en_GB": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Data Literacy)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Data Literacy) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Lecturer (Data Literacy) University-Level Unit: Office of the Provost Faculty/Department-Level Unit: General Education Unit Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 21/08/2026 Job Description Position Overview Applications are invited for the post of Lecturer in Data Literacy at the National University of Singapore (NUS). The successful candidate will be appointed on a full-time, renewable contract under the NUS Educator Track scheme. The post is hosted by the Office of the Provost as administrative host and incubator for the programme, in collaboration with the Department of Mathematics and the Department of Statistics and Data Science. Key Responsibilities Curriculum Design & Delivery: Assist Course Lead in directing the ongoing refinement of content, delivery and assessment for the university-wide general education course for the AI era, GEA1000 Quantitative Reasoning with Data . The course introduces foundational data sense-making and visualisation, drawing on authentic datasets from diverse fields, including science and engineering, healthcare, consumer insights, and public policy. Educational Innovation: Assist the Course Lead in integrating AI and other technologies into teaching pedagogies to enhance student mastery of core data concepts. Curriculum Alignment: Assist the Course Lead in collaborating with academic units across the university to ensure integration between this course and the higher-level data science and analytics courses. Position Details Start date: Immediate, or as soon as practicable, in semester 1 of AY2026/2027 Qualifications Qualifications and Requirements Essential PhD in Statistics, Mathematics, Physics, or closely related quantitative discipline. Desirable attributes Technical Proficiency: Demonstrated expertise in data science, analytics, and practical applications, including proficiency in Excel, and programming languages such as Python or R. Higher Education Teaching: Proven track record of delivering broad-based, common curriculum undergraduate courses. Curriculum Development: Experience in course design, assessment development, and programmatic alignment. Pedagogical Innovation: Experience in leveraging educational technologies, including generative AI, for innovative teaching pedagogies to enhance learning outcomes. Scholarship of Teaching & Learning: Active interest or experience in evidence-based pedagogical research. Please submit the following documents: • Cover letter • Curriculum vitae • Scanned copies of academic degrees • Teaching statement • Two academic or professional referee letters Req ID: 34151 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Education-Associate-I-%28CoRE%29/33882-en_GB": {
      "title": "Education Associate I (CoRE)",
      "description": "Education Associate I (CoRE) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Education Associate I (CoRE) University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 29/07/2026 Job Description Duke-NUS Medical School (Duke-NUS) was established through a landmark collaboration between two world-class institutions; Duke University and National University of Singapore, with the objective of providing innovative education and impactful research that enhance the practice of medicine in Singapore and beyond. The Centre of Regulatory Excellence (CoRE) was established at Duke-NUS in 2014 with the mission of forming regional platforms and networks to grow competencies, build capacity and promote thought leadership in regulatory science and health policy in the Asia Pacific, with a focus on South-East Asia. CoRE has established a strong and highly regarded education portfolio for industry professionals and regulators. The Centre also enables thought leadership and policy innovation in areas of health products regulation, and its expanded scope now includes issues related to global health, health policies and health system strengthening. Its key focus areas are digital health, vaccines & pandemic preparedness, advanced and innovative therapeutics, innovative clinical trials, and medical devices. The roles and responsibilities of the successful candidate would include: - Conduct literature reviews and stakeholder surveys for understanding new trends in health products regulatory science and andragogy Assist in the development of workshop curriculum (learning objectives, programme and assessments), online training materials and case discussions Assist in the implementation of new digital technology in the development and delivery of training materials Assist the operations in conduct of workshops, including student and faculty management and course content management within  Learning Management System Develop and update online training materials e-learning authoring tools while maintaining consistency with instructional design. Build and maintain a network of regulatory technical experts and key opinion leaders, both in Asia Pacific and globally Qualifications Degree in biomedical, life sciences or equivalent with minimum 2 years of relevant working experience in the areas of pharmaceuticals, biologics or medical devices. Experience in and conduct of workshops in regulatory affairs and knowledge of healthcare systems of the ASEAN region will be advantageous. Familiarity with Learning Management Systems (Bright Space, Canvas, LAMS, Elentra or equivalent), instructional design principles or adult learning methodologies Prior experience with the development of training materials using e-leaning authoring tools such as Articulate Storyline, Rise 360, Adobe Captivate or similar platforms Good written and verbal communications skills and the ability to work effectively with internal teams and external technical experts. *We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 33882 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Deputy-Director%2C-Centre-for-Infectious-Disease-Emergency-Response/33818-en_GB": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response",
      "description": "Deputy Director, Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Deputy Director, Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office (Medicine) Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 22/07/2026 Position: Deputy Director, Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response Reporting to:  Programme Director, Professor Dale Fisher Direct Report: As above Job Purpose The Deputy Director provides strategic, scientific, and operational leadership for the Centre for Infectious Disease Emergency Response (CIDER), supporting the Director in advancing the Centre's mission to strengthen educational and operational efforts. The role oversees multidisciplinary programmes spanning outbreak preparedness, epidemiology, surveillance, health systems resilience, translational research, capacity building, and stakeholder engagement at national, regional, and global levels. The Deputy Director ensures the effective coordination of partnerships and emergency response initiatives, while fostering collaboration across NUS, government agencies, healthcare institutions, international organisations, and industry partners to enhance 's and the region's readiness for current and future infectious disease threats. Duties and Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Centre Development Support the Director in developing and implementing the Centre's strategic vision, goals, and operational plans Represent the Centre at institutional, national, regional, and international forums, committees, and working groups. Deputise for the Director as required and provide leadership during periods of increased Infectious Disease Emergency activity. Provide scientific oversight of the Centre's portfolio in infectious diseases, outbreak preparedness, pandemic response, surveillance, and health systems resilience. Develop and lead multidisciplinary initiatives involving faculty, clinicians, scientists, public health practitioners, and external collaborators. Facilitate the translation of research findings into policy, clinical practice, and emergency preparedness frameworks. Identify and secure grant funding from national and international funding agencies. Promote high-quality scientific publications, innovation, and knowledge dissemination. 2. Emergency Preparedness and Response Oversee the development of scenario planning exercises, simulations, and after-action reviews to strengthen preparedness capabilities. Maintain situational awareness of emerging global health threats and develop communication pathways to improve public and professional understanding Establish and implement mechanisms to assist development of the pillars of outbreak response regionally Develop an international network of trained outbreak responders 3. Partnerships and Stakeholder Engagement Build and maintain strategic partnerships with government agencies, healthcare institutions, academic centres, international organisations, NGOs, and industry. Facilitate collaborative projects that advance research, policy development, and emergency preparedness. Strengthen regional and global networks for infectious disease surveillance, capacity development, and rapid response. Serve as a key liaison between the Centre and external stakeholders. Promote the Centre's visibility, impact, and reputation through strategic engagement activities. . 4. Education, Training, and Capacity Building Oversee the development and delivery of educational programmes, professional training, workshops, and simulations related to infectious disease preparedness and response. Mentor faculty, administration, fellows, and students involved in Centre activities. Support workforce development initiatives aimed at strengthening public health and outbreak response capabilities. Foster interdisciplinary learning and collaboration across NUS faculties and external partners 5. Operations and Governance Oversee the effective management of Centre operations, resources, budgets, and personnel. Ensure compliance with NUS policies, funding requirements, governance standards, and regulatory obligations. Develop performance indicators and monitor programme outcomes and impact. Lead risk management, quality assurance, and continuous improvement initiatives. Support recruitment, performance management, and professional development of Centre staff 6. Policy and Knowledge Translation Provide expert advice on infectious disease preparedness, pandemic planning, and health security issues. Lead the preparation of policy briefs, technical reports, and strategic recommendations for stakeholders and decision-makers. Facilitate the translation of scientific evidence into actionable public health interventions. Contribute to national and international discussions on infectious disease preparedness, outbreak response, and health security. Requirements PhD, MD, MBBS with postgraduate qualifications, or equivalent doctorate in infectious diseases, epidemiology, public health, health policy, or a related field. Internationally recognised expertise in infectious diseases, outbreak response, epidemiology, public health preparedness, or health security. Senior leadership experience in academia, healthcare, government, public health agencies, or international organisations. Proven track record in research leadership, grant acquisition, and scholarly publications. Demonstrated experience in managing multidisciplinary teams and complex stakeholder environments. Strong strategic, communication, relationship-building, and organisational skills. Experience contributing to outbreak response. Demonstrably strong international multidisciplinary network For any enquiries: mdcfda@nus.edu.sg (Prof Dale Fisher, NUS) Req ID: 33818 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/DEAN%2C-YONG-LOO-LIN-SCHOOL-OF-MEDICINE%2C-NATIONAL-UNIVERSITY-OF-SINGAPORE/33786-en_GB": {
      "title": "DEAN, YONG LOO LIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE, NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SINGAPORE",
      "description": "DEAN, YONG LOO LIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE, NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SINGAPORE Job Details | National University of Singapore DEAN, YONG LOO LIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE, NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SINGAPORE By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now DEAN, YONG LOO LIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE, NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SINGAPORE University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office (Medicine) Employee Category: Others Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 20/07/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: DEAN, YONG LOO LIN SCHOOL OF MEDICINE, NATIONAL UNIVERSITY OF SINGAPORE University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office (Medicine) Employee Category: Others Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 20/07/2026 Background The National University of Singapore (NUS) invites applications for the post of Dean, Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine. Founded in 1905, the NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine is Singapore’s first and largest medical school, celebrating its 120th year anniversary in 2025. It ranked 13th in the Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026 for Medical and Health and 17th in the Quacquarelli Symonds (QS) World University Rankings by Subject 2026 for Medicine. Today, the school conducts cutting edge research and delivers innovative education, generating high impact solutions that advance the practice of medicine in Singapore and beyond. The School is an integral part of NUS, a comprehensive university with deep interdisciplinary collaborations across engineering, computer science, social science, public health, and other fields. It also benefits from a long-standing partnership  within the National University Health System (NUHS), creating a unique environment that seamlessly combines education, research and patient care. The NUHS ecosystem brings together three tertiary hospitals (National University Hospital, Ng Teng Fong Hospital and Alexandra Hospital), three national specialist centres (National University Heart Centre, National University Cancer Institute and National University Centre for Oral Health), a comprehensive primary care system and three NUS schools in Medicine, Dentistry and Public Health. Together with other healthcare partners and research institutes in Singapore, the school is a key contributor to Singapore’s vibrant biomedical ecosystem. For more information, please visit the website: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine . Profile of Candidate As the Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine advances its global leadership in medical education, biomedical research, and healthcare innovation, NUS seeks a visionary and people-centred leader who can articulate a compelling strategic direction for the School; foster an inclusive, collaborative, and high-performing academic culture; strengthen partnerships across the University, healthcare system, and international community; attract, develop, and retain outstanding and diverse faculty, students, and staff; and lead the School in addressing emerging opportunities in healthcare, technology, and medical education. The Dean must be able to inspire trust, exercise integrity and sound judgement, unite the School around a shared vision, and possess an exemplary scholarly record and international reputation suitable for appointment as a tenured Full Professor in the School. NUS is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion in its community. We encourage applications by individuals who embody and embrace these values. Submission The Search Committee welcomes applications and nominations of suitable candidates. Application materials should include a full Curriculum Vitae and a broad vision statement for the School. Applications, enquiries or nominations should be sent by 31 October 2026 to: Professor HO Ghim Wei Vice-Provost (Academic Affairs) Chair, Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Dean Search Committee National University of Singapore c/o Ms Dolly Teo YLLSOM Dean Search Committee Secretariat E-mail: dollyteo@nus.edu.sg All nominations and applications will be kept in the strictest confidence. We appreciate your kind understanding that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 33786 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/InstructorAssistant-Professor-%28Teaching%29/33768-en_GB": {
      "title": "Scope of Position",
      "description": "Instructor/Assistant Professor (Teaching) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Instructor/Assistant Professor (Teaching) University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Office of Education Employee Category: Others Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 16/07/2026 Scope of Position This faculty position focuses primarily on the teaching and facilitation of clinical skills and foundational medical education within the MD Programme. The role emphasizes direct student engagement through simulation-based education, procedural skills training, communication skills, clinical reasoning, and Team-Based Learning (TBL) facilitation in Phase I. The faculty member will also contribute to curriculum development through participation in curriculum mapping, review processes, and the refinement of teaching activities. The role works closely with the Associate Dean of the MD Programme and collaborates with faculty and staff across the MD Programme Department. Opportunities are available to engage in medical education scholarship under the guidance of senior faculty. Job Description Clinical and Foundational Teaching (Primary) Deliver clinical skills teaching in areas including procedural skills, communication skills, history-taking, physical examination, and clinical reasoning. Plan and run simulation-based learning activities in close collaboration with the Simulation Lead, contribute to the development of faculty guides, and support clinical faculty in delivering simulation sessions. Facilitate Team-Based Learning (TBL) sessions in Phase I, including readiness assurance tests and case-based application exercises. Provide timely formative feedback and coaching to support learner development. Support knowledge exam preparation sessions and other structured learning activities as required. Collaborate with the Clinical Performance Centre (CPC) and course leads to ensure effective delivery of teaching. Curriculum Development and Support Contribute to the development and implementation of learning activities aligned with curriculum objectives. Participate in curriculum mapping and periodic curriculum review. Educational Scholarship Participate in medical education research and scholarly activities within the MD Programme Department and/or the Office of Education. Contribute to presentations, abstracts, or publications related to teaching and learning in medical education. Remain current with trends and innovations in medical education and apply evidence-informed practices to teaching. Service to School and Community Participate in committees and task forces within the Medical Education and MD Programme Offices as needed. Participate in and provide support for faculty development activities and other educational initiatives within the institution. Collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, and administrative units in the delivery of the MD Programme. Support other curriculum-related tasks as assigned by the Associate Dean or MD Programme leadership. Support evaluation and iterative improvement of teaching sessions. Qualifications Medical degree (MBBS or equivalent) is required. Minimum 4–5 years of clinical practice experience. Experience in clinical skills teaching and/or TBL facilitation. Experience in simulation-based or procedural skills education is strongly preferred. Strong interpersonal communication skills and decision-making acumen. Excellent command of English. Ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary teams and contribute to strategic educational goals. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team, ensuring smooth collaboration and productivity. Collaborate with course leads to ensure alignment between teaching activities and assessment components. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 33768 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Professor-Associate-Professor%2C-Dept-of-Management-and-Organisation/33745-en_GB": {
      "title": "OPEN-RANK, TENURE-TRACK POSITIONS",
      "description": "Professor / Associate Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Professor / Associate Professor, Dept of Management and Organisation University-Level Unit: School of Business Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Management And Organisation Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 15/07/2026 OPEN-RANK, TENURE-TRACK POSITIONS Position: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor (tenure track) with a preference to hire a mid-career or senior candidate. Specialization: Human Resource Management / Organizational Behavior (broadly defined). We also welcome applicants trained in Industrial–Organizational Psychology, Social Psychology, Behavioral Economics, and related fields whose research speaks to HR/OB topics. The School and Environment Consistently ranked #1 in Asia, and AACSB / EQUIS accredited. Generous research support: competitive salary and benefits, start-up research grant,research assistants, behavioral labs, database subscriptions, and internal fundingschemes. Teaching load: 2 + 0 in the first two years for Assistant Professors; 3 + 0 thereafter. Subsidized, university-allocated housing (up to 9 years, subject to eligibility). Faculty publish regularly in AMJ, AMR, JAP, OBHDP, Org Science, PNAS, and othertop outlets. Singapore is a stable, safe, cosmopolitan city-state where English is an officiallanguage and the quality of life rivals that of major North American and European cities. Responsibilities Produce high-impact scholarly research. Teach in our Undergraduate, MSc, MBA, EMBA, PhD, and Executive Educationprograms. Supervise doctoral students and contribute to a vibrant research culture in a diverseand inclusive community. Required Qualifications A PhD in Management, OB, HRM, I/O Psychology, or a closely related discipline. A strong track record of publishing in top-tier journals. Commitment to excellent, innovative teaching. Application Procedure To ensure full consideration, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and brief statements of research and teaching interests to Jen Lee at mno-recruitment@nus.edu.sg, using the subject line “OB/HR Position,”. The search committee will be scheduling meeting times during the Academy of Management Annual Meeting. If you are interested in being considered for a meeting, please contact the Chair of the Search Committee, Hemant Kakkar, at hemant_kakkar@nus.edu.sg. Req ID: 33745 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer-%28The-Yeo-Boon-Khim-Mind-Science-Centre-%28MSC%29/31985-en_GB": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (The Yeo Boon Khim Mind Science Centre (MSC)",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (The Yeo Boon Khim Mind Science Centre (MSC) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (The Yeo Boon Khim Mind Science Centre (MSC) University-Level Unit: Yeo Boon Khim Mind Science Centre Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Yeo Boon Khim Mind Science Centre Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 14/07/2026 . The Yeo Boon Khim Mind Science Centre (MSC) at the National University of Singapore is dedicated to advancing mind science through education, applied research, and real-world impact. It aims to strengthen mental health and wellbeing at every life stage. The Centre researches youth and adolescent resilience, community and caregiver mental health, workplace wellbeing, and digital interventions. MSC emphasises prevention and develops evidence-based, scalable programmes that translate mind science into education, professional practice, and policy for healthcare, communities, and society. The appointee will be based at the MSC and will work closely with the Centre Director and interdisciplinary faculty across psychology, psychiatry, and public health to contribute to high-quality postgraduate and professional programmes. The position may be offered at Lecturer or Senior Lecturer level, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The appointment will be on a fixed-term basis with the possibility of renewal if the performance is satisfactory. Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: Build and maintain expertise in mind science and clinical psychology–related domains, aligned with MSC’s focus on prevention, resilience, mental wellbeing, and applied mental health. Contribute to the design, development, delivery, and evaluation of postgraduate and professional education programmes, including blended and online learning formats. Develop curriculum content and learning materials grounded in psychological theory, clinical evidence, and applied practice. Teach and facilitate learning activities related to clinical psychology, mental health assessment, intervention principles, resilience, and applied mind science, as appropriate to the programme. Participate in programme evaluation, quality assurance, and continuous improvement of educational offerings. To provide clinical psychology training, supervision, and mentoring To build and strengthen a professional network, seek out new connections to support the programme's placement component. To champion the accreditation of the Master’s in Clinical Mental Health and Psychotherapy Collaborate with colleagues on interdisciplinary research, implementation studies, and translation of evidence into educational and community programmes. Contribute to outreach and engagement with professional bodies, community partners, and affiliated institutions to strengthen MSC’s education and training network. Support scholarly dissemination, including preparation of educational reports, analyses, and contributions to publications where relevant. Perform other duties incidental to the role in support of the Centre’s education, research, and outreach objectives. Requirements Applicants should have: A PhD/Doctorate in Clinical Psychology, or Master's in Clinical Psychology or related disciplines Registered Clinical Psychologist with the Singapore Psychological Society Formal training and/or demonstrated expertise in clinical psychology or applied psychological practice, relevant to education and training. Ability to teach at postgraduate or professional levels in areas related to clinical psychology, mental health, and mind science. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively within interdisciplinary teams. Strong organisational skills and the ability to work independently while managing multiple academic and programme-related responsibilities. Proven capability in leading the educational programme with strong administrative skills Interested applicants are invited to apply directly at the NUS Career Portal, along with a letter of application and their full curriculum vitae. The selection process would be on a rolling basis until a candidate is appointed. Req ID: 31985 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Lecturer-%28Engineering-Design-and-Innovation-Centre%29/20806-en_GB": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Engineering Design and Innovation Centre)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Engineering Design and Innovation Centre) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Lecturer (Engineering Design and Innovation Centre) University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean's Office (College of Design & Eng) Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 08/07/2026 Job Description The Engineering Design and Innovation Centre (EDIC) at the National University of Singapore (NUS) is seeking an educator-track faculty member to lead and supervise multi-disciplinary projects and to teach courses at the undergraduate and Master’s level. EDIC offers exciting project-based learning programmes (the undergraduate Innovation and Design Programme and the Master of Science in Engineering Design and Innovation) that aim to train engineering graduates of the future. It aspires to be the thought leader in design and innovation and wishes to attract top passionate educators who are excited by this opportunity. Candidates with at least one of the following expertise are eligible to apply: •    Experience in entrepreneurship and innovation. •    Strong skills in robotics / electrical / electronic firmware / mechanical design and development. •    Experience in UI / UX / HCI / AR / VR. •    Experience with data analytics and data driven design. •    Experience in developing mechanical systems related to vehicular technology (e.g. autonomous vehicles, energy efficient vehicles, etc.). •    Experience in teaching design thinking or industrial design will be an added advantage. Aside from experience in any of the above areas, he/she should have a strong passion in engaging and nurturing students and be ready to take ownership of the projects. A demonstrated track record in leading bold and creative projects would be a definite advantage. Qualifications While we expect the candidate to have earned a Ph.D. degree in either Mechanical / Electrical / Computer Engineering, we also welcome applicants from other engineering or related disciplines, as well as applicants with a Master’s degree who have knowledge or real experience in starting an enterprise. The candidate is expected to supervise multi-disciplinary groups of students who generally have interests in entrepreneurship. More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: College of Design and Engineering Department : Dean's Office (College of Design & Eng) Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 20806 Req ID: 20806 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Professor-%28Epidemiology%29/26529-en_GB": {
      "title": "Professor (Epidemiology)",
      "description": "Professor (Epidemiology) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Professor (Epidemiology) University-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 03/07/2026 Job Description The National University of Singapore – which is the top ranked university in Asia – is recruiting full-time Professors for the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health (SSHSPH). All positions are tenure-track appointment (i.e. appointees are given fixed contracts for up to 7 years, with the goal of obtaining tenured appointments at the end of this period). In additional to an attractive salary and benefits package, new faculty members are eligible for a start-up grant to initiate their independent stream of research and subsidised university accommodation, subject to prevailing terms and conditions. Researchers in the following areas are particularly encouraged to apply: Investigating the distribution and determinants of non-communicable and infectious diseases in populations and applying epidemiological methods to understand disease patterns and identify risk factors. Developing and applying mathematical models to predict disease trends and evaluate the potential impact of interventions, supporting the formulation of effective public health strategies and policies. Simulating disease transmission dynamics and intervention scenarios to assess the potential impacts of public health interventions, enhancing preparedness and response strategies for disease outbreaks. Engaging with SSHSPH’s large-scale cohort studies, such as the Singapore Chinese Health Study (SCHS) and the Singapore Multi-Ethnic Cohort (MEC) Study, to contribute to the development and utilisation of these cohort studies and to conduct translational epidemiological research that informs the development of effective public health interventions. Job Responsibilities R esearch respons i b ili t i es i nc l ude developing and establishing collaborative research proposals with NUS faculty for extramural funding. SSHSPH has several large-scale cohort studies including the Singapore Chinese Health Study and the Multi Ethnic Cohort Study. Applicants are expected to contribute to the development and use of these cohort studies and/or to conduct translational epidemiological research that informs the development of public health interventions. Teaching responsibilities include the development and teaching of courses in epidemiology and other areas of public health and the supervision of graduate students. Qualifications A recognised Doctoral degree in a relevant discipline with a strong post-doctoral professional and/or academic record; OR a qualified medical professional with postgraduate specialisation in occupational health, occupational medicine, or preventive medicine. Proven track record of publishing in high-impact international peer-reviewed journals. Experience in leading independent research studies or components within larger research programmes, and/or developing, leading, implementing and evaluating projects and programmes. Ability to generate and sustain an independent stream of research funding. Ability to teach public health courses at various levels (undergraduate, graduate and lifelong learners). Ability to work within multidisciplinary teams. Ability to work with and teach culturally diverse audiences. More Information To apply, please submit a cover letter specifying your research and/or teaching interests and experience, your curriculum vitae, names and contact details of 3 references. For more information on NUS please visit: www.nus.edu.sg . For more information about the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health please visit www.sph.nus.edu.sg . Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Req ID: 26529 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Associate-Professor-%28Epidemiology%29/23560-en_GB": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Epidemiology)",
      "description": "Associate Professor (Epidemiology) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Associate Professor (Epidemiology) University-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 03/07/2026 Associate Professor (Epidemiology) The National University of Singapore – which is the top ranked university in Asia – is recruiting full-time Associate Professors/Professors for the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health (SSHSPH). All positions are tenure-track appointment (i.e. appointees are given fixed contracts for up to 7 years, with the goal of obtaining tenured appointments at the end of this period). In additional to an attractive salary and benefits package, new faculty members are eligible for a start-up grant to initiate their independent stream of research and subsidised university accommodation, subject to prevailing terms and conditions. Researchers in the following areas are particularly encouraged to apply: Epidemiological research with a focus on molecular epidemiology, nutritional epidemiology, social epidemiology or behavioral epidemiology. Epidemiological research on obesity, type 2 diabetes, and cardiovascular diseases. Epidemiological research on cancer and non-communicable diseases. Qualifications Required qualifications are: an earned doctoral degree in a relevant discipline a strong track record of publications in international peer-reviewed journals ability to contribute to courses relevant to epidemiology and public health Responsibilities R esearch respons i b ili t i es i nc l ude developing and establishing collaborative research proposals with NUS faculty for extramural funding. SSHSPH has several large-scale cohort studies including the Singapore Chinese Health Study and the Multi Ethnic Cohort Study. Applicants are expected to contribute to the development and use of these cohort studies and/or to conduct translational epidemiological research that informs the development of public health interventions. Teaching responsibilities include the development and teaching of courses in epidemiology and other areas of public health and the supervision of graduate students. More Information To apply, please submit a cover letter specifying your research and/or teaching interests and experience, your curriculum vitae, names and contact details of 3 references. For more information on NUS, please visit: www.nus.edu.sg. For more information about the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health, please visit www.sph.nus.edu.sg. Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Req ID: 23560 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Associate-Professor-%28Cancer-Science-Institute%29/28471-en_GB": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Cancer Science Institute)",
      "description": "Associate Professor (Cancer Science Institute) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Associate Professor (Cancer Science Institute) University-Level Unit: Cancer Science Institute of Singapore Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Administration Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 01/07/2026 Job Description The Cancer Science Institute of Singapore (CSI) at the National University of Singapore (NUS) invites applications for multiple tenure-track and tenured faculty positions at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level. CSI is a globally recognized research institute committed to advancing the frontiers of cancer biology, immunology, and translational medicine . With a mission to transform cancer detection, treatment, and prevention, our purpose-built institute leverages state-of-the-art infrastructure, multidisciplinary expertise, and strong clinical partnerships to deliver impactful, patient-centered research. Our scientific community spans biological, computational, and engineering disciplines, focusing on the unique cancer challenges of Asia while contributing meaningfully to global cancer research. We are seeking exceptional, visionary scientists to join our expanding faculty and shape new research directions that complement our existing strengths. Candidates from all areas of cancer research are welcome, with particular interest in the following domains: Computational Biology of Cancer Evolution Cancer Immunology and Immunotherapy Epithelial Cancer Biology We welcome applications from scientists who meet the following criteria: A Ph.D. and/or M.D. in a relevant field A strong track record of research excellence, commensurate with career stage A distinguished portfolio of publications, research leadership, and scientific contributions in cancer research Demonstrated success in securing competitive research funding and leading multidisciplinary research initiatives Successful candidates will join a vibrant and collaborative research environment with access to: World-class laboratory facilities and advanced core technologies Competitive start-up packages and institutional research funding A globally benchmarked salary and benefits package Extensive opportunities for interdisciplinary collaborations across NUS and with international academic and industry partners Application Documents To apply, please submit the following documents: Cover Letter Describe your background, research interests, and how your work aligns with CSI’s mission and strategic priorities. Comprehensive Curriculum Vitae Include a complete list of publications, grants awarded, honors, and leadership roles. Statement of Key Achievements and Future Research Plans (up to 1500 words) Highlight your most significant contributions to cancer research. Articulate your future research vision and potential synergies with CSI. Three References Provide contact details of three senior scientists who can speak to your qualifications and research impact. Req ID: 28471 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Cancer-Science-Institute%29/30188-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute) University-Level Unit: Cancer Science Institute of Singapore Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Administration Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 01/07/2026 Job Description The Cancer Science Institute of Singapore (CSI) is seeking outstanding and visionary researchers for multiple faculty positions, ranging from Assistant to Full Professor . As a globally recognized leader with a reputation of excellence in cancer biology, immunology, and translational medicine, CSI is dedicated to transforming cancer detection, treatment, and prevention to improve patient outcomes. Our institute is purpose-built for cancer research and integrates cutting-edge technology, multidisciplinary approaches, and strong clinical collaborations to achieve groundbreaking discoveries. Our work spans the biological, computational, and engineering sciences, with a mission to address the unique cancer landscape of Asia while contributing to global progress. We are expanding our faculty to complement existing strengths and seed new, strategic directions in cancer research. We invite applications from exceptional scientists working in any area of cancer research, with particular interest in the following fields: Computational Biology of Cancer Evolution Cancer Immunology and Immunotherapy Epithelial Cancer Biology Successful candidates will join a dynamic, collaborative environment and gain access to: State-of-the-art laboratories and world-class core facilities Generous start-up support and institutional research funding A competitive salary package aligned with global benchmarks Opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaborations within NUS and with global academic and industry partners Candidates should possess and demonstrate the following: A PhD and/or M.D. degree in a relevant discipline An established record of research excellence, with international competitiveness for their career stage A distinguished track record of research, publications, and leadership in cancer research Proven ability to secure funding and drive impactful, multidisciplinary research programs Application Documents To facilitate the application process, Candidates are invited to submit the following: Cover Letter Describe your background, expertise, and alignment with CSI's mission Comprehensive CV Include a full publication list, grants, awards, and leadership roles Key Achievements and Future Plans (up to 1500 words) Summarize your pivotal contributions to cancer research Outline your future research goals and potential synergies with CSI References Contact details of three senior colleagues willing to provide letters of reference Req ID: 30188 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
