ncer Immunology and Immunotherapy Epithelial Cancer Biology Successful candidates will join a dynamic, collaborative environment and gain access to: State-of-the-art laboratories and world-class core facilities Generous start-up support and institutional research funding A competitive salary package aligned with global benchmarks Opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaborations within NUS and with global academic and industry partners Candidates should possess and demonstrate the following: A PhD and/or M.D. degree in a relevant discipline An established record of research excellence, with international competitiveness for their career stage A distinguished track record of research, publications, and leadership in cancer research Proven ability to secure funding and drive impactful, multidisciplinary research programs Application Documents To facilitate the application process, Candidates are invited to submit the following: Cover Letter Describe your background, expertise, and alignment with CSI's mission Comprehensive CV Include a full publication list, grants, awards, and leadership roles Key Achievements and Future Plans (up to 1500 words) Summarize your pivotal contributions to cancer research Outline your future research goals and potential synergies with CSI References Contact details of three senior colleagues willing to provide letters of reference Req ID: 28465 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Director-of-Advanced-Electron-Microscopy-Facility/33568-en_GB": {
      "title": "Director of Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility",
      "description": "Director of Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Director of Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility University-Level Unit: Office of the Deputy President(Res&Tech) Faculty/Department-Level Unit: S9 Advanced Microscopy Facility Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 01/07/2026 Job Description NUS seeks to appoint a globally recognised scientific leader to serve as Director of the Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility, a flagship, university-level platform integrating state-of-the-art capabilities across materials science and life sciences. The Director will shape the facility into a globally leading centre for atomic-scale imaging and analysis, driving both frontier research and national-level capabilities. The Advanced Electron Microscopy Facility is a newly established university-level microscopy facility at NUS combining the state-of-the-art Electron and Scanning Tunnelling Microscopes for both the materials and life sciences. It is a centralised shared facility serving the research community at NUS, in Singapore, and beyond. It enables high-resolution 3D structure determination (CryoEM, FIB-SEM) and materials characterisation (such as AC-EM and STM). The facility aims to provide researchers with a unique competitive edge and students with excellent education and training opportunities. Driven by research of its members, it aims at being a world-leading research facility in Materials Science EM and Life Science cryoEM. Key Responsibilities Provide strategic leadership and direction to position the facility as a hub for large-scale international collaborations and flagship programmes. Set appropriate medium- and long-term research directions aligned with the facilities. Lead large, multi‑year research programmes by setting scientific directions and coordinating stakeholders. Set clear targets and user satisfaction measures. Develop the facility roadmap for future upgrades, new platforms, and capacity planning. Develop cost-recovery models (set internal/external rates), manage budgets and procurement. Ensure compliance with laboratory safety requirements and all NUS policies. Implement good data management practices. Qualifications NUS seeks to hire an outstanding research leader with strong relevant experience, possibly integrating material and life sciences EM. The appointment is anticipated at the Full Professor level and is expected to sustain an internationally leading research programme aligned with the facility’s strengths. Requirements Currently holding a faculty position with experience in life sciences, materials science and engineering, physics, or a related field. Evidence of significant core facility leadership. Proven track record of excellent publications and scientific contributions in the electron microscopy field. Distinguished records of research and administrative experience, and evidence of excellent leadership, interpersonal, and communication skills. Proven ability to lead teams, manage budgets, generate consistent external funding, run service operations, and deal with governments and corporate organisations locally and internationally. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 33568 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Biostatistics-and-Modelling%29%2C-Saw-Swee-Hock-School-of-Public-Health%2C-NUS/29949-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Biostatistics and Modelling), Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health, NUS",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Biostatistics and Modelling), Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health, NUS Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Biostatistics and Modelling), Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health, NUS University-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 25/06/2026 Job Description The National University of Singapore – which is the top ranked university in Asia – is recruiting full-time Assistant Professor(s) for the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health (SSHSPH) on the tenure track. For the tenure track, appointees are given fixed contracts for up to 7 years, with the goal of obtaining tenure at the end of this period. In addition to an attractive salary and benefits package, new faculty members may be eligible for a start-up grant to initiate their independent stream of research and subsidised university accommodation. The School is seeking to hire one or more biostatisticians, ideally those working on public health applications. The positions are specifically for faculty to work in the Biostatistics and Modelling Domain (BSMD) of SSHSPH. Researchers with existing research activities applying statistical methods in cancer, epidemiological studies, health promotion, physical activity, nutrition and primary care are particularly encouraged to apply. Qualifications Requirements: A recognized Doctoral degree in a relevant discipline with a strong post-doctoral research record; Track record of publishing in international peer-reviewed journals; Ability to generate and maintain an independent stream of funding; Ability to teach public health courses at both undergraduate and graduate levels; Ability to work in multidisciplinary teams; Ability to work with culturally diverse populations. Additional requirements to be appointed to the tenure track: Track record of publishing in high-impact international peer-reviewed journals; Experience in leading independent research studies; Ability to develop an internationally renowned research programme. Responsibilities Responsibilities include: establishing an independent research programme; providing statistical support for collaborative, multidisciplinary research; course design and teaching; and graduate student advising. To apply, please submit a cover letter specifying your research and teaching interests and experience, your curriculum vitae, and names and contacts of 3 references . For more information on NUS please visit: www.nus.edu.sg . For more information about the Saw Swee Hock School of Public Health please visit www.sph.nus.edu.sg . Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. Req ID: 29949 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28CBDS%29/32996-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (CBDS)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (CBDS) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (CBDS) University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Office of Research Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 19/06/2026 Job Description Duke-NUS Medical School (Duke-NUS), Singapore’s only graduate-entry medical school, is a landmark collaboration between two world-ranking institutions of higher education – Duke University and the National University of Singapore (NUS). Duke-NUS provides innovative education and impactful research to advance medicine and improve lives. Through our strategic partnership with Singapore Health Services (SingHealth), the largest public healthcare cluster in Singapore, the SingHealth Duke-NUS Academic Medical Centre fosters cutting-edge collaborations in translational and clinical research, driving discoveries and solutions to global healthcare challenges. The Duke-NUS Centre for Biomedical Data Science (CBDS) serves as a central hub for Duke-NUS faculty specialising in Biostatistics, Bioinformatics, Systems Biology, Artificial Intelligence (AI), and other quantitative and data-driven sciences. CBDS functions as a strategic platform for cutting-edge research, education, and services in Precision Medicine, data science, AI, and biomedical computation, building on existing institutional initiatives such as DAISI. CBDS is seeking to fill a tenure track faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. Key Responsibilities Lead an innovative research programme in AI/ML, with applications in Precision Medicine, clinical research, omics, imaging, or population health. Translate and implement advanced analytic approaches (e.g., multimodal AI) into clinical/biomedical settings with SingHealth/NUS collaborators. Engage in collaborative research with clinicians, biomedical researchers, and statisticians across SingHealth, NUS, Duke University, and national initiatives such as Singapore’s National Precision Medicine Programme and Precision Health Research, Singapore (PRECISE). Mentor and supervise PhD students, promoting local capacity and excellence in methodology and translational AI. Actively contribute to grant acquisition, research leadership, and dissemination of results through high-impact publications. Support teaching in Biostatistics, Health Data Science, and related program. Job Requirements PhD in Statistics, Biostatistics, Computer Science, or a related quantitative discipline, with strong evidence of applying AI in biomedical/clinical contexts or relevant industry experience in biopharma or related sectors. Proven publication record in reputable journals and recognition for methodological and/or applied contributions in healthcare AI. Demonstrated track record in securing and contributing to research grants as both Principal Investigator and Co-Investigator. Excellent problem-solving skills and ability to communicate effectively across disciplines. Demonstrated experience with multidisciplinary projects, particularly at the intersection of method development and clinical/population health application. Prior teaching and supervision experience at the graduate level is preferred. Faculty recruits will be provided with a competitive salary, research space, and start-up funding commensurate with their rank and proposed research programme. Interested candidates should send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, and the names of three referees in support of their application via email at hr@duke-nus.edu.sg and attention it to: Administrative Chair Search Committee, CBDS Duke-NUS Medical School Applications will be open until the position is filled. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. More Information Location: Outram Campus Organization: Duke-NUS Medical School Department : Office of Research Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 32996 Req ID: 32996 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer%2C-Tembusu-College/33414-en_GB": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Tembusu College",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Tembusu College Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Tembusu College University-Level Unit: Tembusu College Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Tembusu College Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 18/06/2026 Job Description Tembusu College, National University of Singapore invites applications for College Fellows, to be appointed as Senior Lecturer or Lecturer on the Educator Track. Applicants from all academic disciplines with interdisciplinary experience and expertise are welcome. Tembusu College offers an array of interdisciplinary Year 1 and Year 2 level seminar-style course as an alternative pathway to fulfil undergraduate students' General Education graduation requirements. Fellows are expected to design, lead or co-lead seminar(s) in an interdisciplinary education environment. In addition to formal teaching in the classroom, Fellows are actively engaged in out-of-classroom teaching and learning activities. They also support the running of the College through service contributions and leading on key administrative tasks. We are interested in candidates who are genuinely interested in and committed to supporting students in their holistic growth, individually as well as members of community in a living-learning context. This appointment will commence in AY2026/2027 Semester 2. Qualifications About Tembusu College Established in 2011, Tembusu College is one of four residential colleges at NUS University Town. Besides formal curriculum, students engage in vibrant student life activities. These include a wide variety of interest groups from sports to arts and events with faculty members, visiting scholars, and distinguished individuals in informal dialogues. Job Requirements PhD, or one close to completion with relevant teaching experience. Enthusiasm and aptitude for inter-disciplinary teaching. Administration and events management experience. Willingness to engage and mentor students in a residential living and learning programme. Desire to pursue a career as an educator who is reflective, and is interested to engage in scholarly inquiry in teaching and learning. Application Procedure Applicants should apply online via NUS Careers at http://www.nus.edu.sg/careers/ (Academic and Research Positions). Applications must include the following documents: Cover letter (in pdf form) Curriculum Vitae (in pdf form) Document not exceeding 1,500 words that includes (in pdf form) teaching philosophy teaching experience administrative experience research activities (if any) community service or engagement involvement in student development beyond the classroom Three letters of reference from referees who can speak to your teaching and/or research, as well as your experience with student development and administration. The cover letter or CV should include names, designation, and contact details of the three referees. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Shortlisted candidates may be required to submit additional documents for review. Closing date : 15 July 2026 Req ID: 33414 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Professor%2C-Strategy-and-Policy/33363-en_GB": {
      "title": "Professor, Strategy and Policy",
      "description": "Professor, Strategy and Policy Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Professor, Strategy and Policy University-Level Unit: School of Business Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Strategy And Policy Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 16/06/2026 Job Overview The Department of Strategy and Policy at NUS Business School invites applications from Strategy / Management of Technology / Entrepreneurship scholars for tenure-track and tenured positions (all ranks). Candidates should hold a Ph.D. or be near completion. Selection for full / associate ranks will be based on an established publication record and proven teaching experience. Selection for the assistant rank will be based on potential for publications in top journals and effective teaching. About NUS The National University of Singapore (NUS) is Singapore’s flagship university, which offers a global approach to education, research and entrepreneurship, with a focus on Asian perspectives and expertise. We have 16 colleges, faculties and schools with more than 40,000 students from 100 countries enriching our vibrant and diverse community. We have also established our NUS Overseas Colleges programme in more than 15 cities around the world. For more information on NUS, please visit www.nus.edu.sg . About NUS Business School The National University of Singapore (NUS) Business School is known for providing management thought leadership from an Asian perspective, enabling its students and corporate partners to leverage global knowledge and Asian insights. The school has consistently received top rankings in the Asia-Pacific region by independent publications and agencies, such as The Financial Times, Economist Intelligence Unit, and QS Top MBA, in recognition of the quality of its programmes, faculty research and graduates. The Department of Strategy and Policy ( https://bschool.nus.edu.sg/strategy-policy/) numbers about 30 faculty members representing more than 13 nationalities, who regularly publish in major international journals including the Strategic Management Journal, Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Administrative Science Quarterly, Management Science, and Organization Science . For more information, please visit bschool.nus.edu.sg. Application Procedures We offer a conducive research environment with generous research funding, as well as competitive remuneration and benefits. Prospective applicants should submit the following materials: (1) a cover letter outlining their research interests and teaching experience; (2) curriculum vitae (CV); (3) samples of research papers or a job market paper; and (4) three letters of recommendation (for junior candidates). For junior applicants, all application materials should be submitted via email to bprecruit@nus.edu.sg no later than September 1, 2026 , to receive full consideration. Mid-career applicants have no fixed deadline and are encouraged to apply at their earliest convenience. Preliminary interviews will be conducted at the Academy of Management (AOM) Annual Meeting in Philadelphia. While participation in these interviews is not mandatory, applicants who wish to be considered for an AOM interview should submit their CV by July 10, 2026 . Commitment to Fair and Inclusive Employment We believe in creating a workplace that values diversity, promotes equal opportunities, and fosters an inclusive culture where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates, and select faculty solely based on merit and job-related criteria, such as skills, experience, and ability to perform the job. We do not discriminate on the basis of age, ethnicity, gender, religion, marital status, family responsibilities, or disability, and are committed to ensuring a fair and equitable recruitment process for all. We continue to uphold these principles and strive to create a workplace that is welcoming, respectful, and supportive for all. Req ID: 33363 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Associate-Professor%2C-Strategy-and-Policy/33362-en_GB": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Strategy and Policy",
      "description": "Associate Professor, Strategy and Policy Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Associate Professor, Strategy and Policy University-Level Unit: School of Business Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Strategy And Policy Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 16/06/2026 Job Overview The Department of Strategy and Policy at NUS Business School invites applications from Strategy / Management of Technology / Entrepreneurship scholars for tenure-track and tenured positions (all ranks). Candidates should hold a Ph.D. or be near completion. Selection for full / associate ranks will be based on an established publication record and proven teaching experience. Selection for the assistant rank will be based on potential for publications in top journals and effective teaching. About NUS The National University of Singapore (NUS) is Singapore’s flagship university, which offers a global approach to education, research and entrepreneurship, with a focus on Asian perspectives and expertise. We have 16 colleges, faculties and schools with more than 40,000 students from 100 countries enriching our vibrant and diverse community. We have also established our NUS Overseas Colleges programme in more than 15 cities around the world. For more information on NUS, please visit www.nus.edu.sg . About NUS Business School The National University of Singapore (NUS) Business School is known for providing management thought leadership from an Asian perspective, enabling its students and corporate partners to leverage global knowledge and Asian insights. The school has consistently received top rankings in the Asia-Pacific region by independent publications and agencies, such as The Financial Times, Economist Intelligence Unit, and QS Top MBA, in recognition of the quality of its programmes, faculty research and graduates. The Department of Strategy and Policy ( https://bschool.nus.edu.sg/strategy-policy/) numbers about 30 faculty members representing more than 13 nationalities, who regularly publish in major international journals including the Strategic Management Journal, Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Administrative Science Quarterly, Management Science, and Organization Science . For more information, please visit bschool.nus.edu.sg. Application Procedures We offer a conducive research environment with generous research funding, as well as competitive remuneration and benefits. Prospective applicants should submit the following materials: (1) a cover letter outlining their research interests and teaching experience; (2) curriculum vitae (CV); (3) samples of research papers or a job market paper; and (4) three letters of recommendation (for junior candidates). For junior applicants, all application materials should be submitted via email to bprecruit@nus.edu.sg no later than September 1, 2026 , to receive full consideration. Mid-career applicants have no fixed deadline and are encouraged to apply at their earliest convenience. Preliminary interviews will be conducted at the Academy of Management (AOM) Annual Meeting in Philadelphia. While participation in these interviews is not mandatory, applicants who wish to be considered for an AOM interview should submit their CV by July 10, 2026 . Commitment to Fair and Inclusive Employment We believe in creating a workplace that values diversity, promotes equal opportunities, and fosters an inclusive culture where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates, and select faculty solely based on merit and job-related criteria, such as skills, experience, and ability to perform the job. We do not discriminate on the basis of age, ethnicity, gender, religion, marital status, family responsibilities, or disability, and are committed to ensuring a fair and equitable recruitment process for all. We continue to uphold these principles and strive to create a workplace that is welcoming, respectful, and supportive for all. Req ID: 33362 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor%2C-Strategy-and-Policy/33359-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Strategy and Policy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Strategy and Policy Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor, Strategy and Policy University-Level Unit: School of Business Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Strategy And Policy Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 16/06/2026 Job Overview The Department of Strategy and Policy at NUS Business School invites applications from Strategy / Management of Technology / Entrepreneurship scholars for tenure-track and tenured positions (all ranks). Candidates should hold a Ph.D. or be near completion. Selection for full / associate ranks will be based on an established publication record and proven teaching experience. Selection for the assistant rank will be based on potential for publications in top journals and effective teaching. About NUS The National University of Singapore (NUS) is Singapore’s flagship university, which offers a global approach to education, research and entrepreneurship, with a focus on Asian perspectives and expertise. We have 16 colleges, faculties and schools with more than 40,000 students from 100 countries enriching our vibrant and diverse community. We have also established our NUS Overseas Colleges programme in more than 15 cities around the world. For more information on NUS, please visit www.nus.edu.sg . About NUS Business School The National University of Singapore (NUS) Business School is known for providing management thought leadership from an Asian perspective, enabling its students and corporate partners to leverage global knowledge and Asian insights. The school has consistently received top rankings in the Asia-Pacific region by independent publications and agencies, such as The Financial Times, Economist Intelligence Unit, and QS Top MBA, in recognition of the quality of its programmes, faculty research and graduates. The Department of Strategy and Policy ( https://bschool.nus.edu.sg/strategy-policy/) numbers about 30 faculty members representing more than 13 nationalities, who regularly publish in major international journals including the Strategic Management Journal, Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Administrative Science Quarterly, Management Science, and Organization Science . For more information, please visit bschool.nus.edu.sg. Application Procedures We offer a conducive research environment with generous research funding, as well as competitive remuneration and benefits. Prospective applicants should submit the following materials: (1) a cover letter outlining their research interests and teaching experience; (2) curriculum vitae (CV); (3) samples of research papers or a job market paper; and (4) three letters of recommendation (for junior candidates). For junior applicants, all application materials should be submitted via email to bprecruit@nus.edu.sg no later than September 1, 2026 , to receive full consideration. Mid-career applicants have no fixed deadline and are encouraged to apply at their earliest convenience. Preliminary interviews will be conducted at the Academy of Management (AOM) Annual Meeting in Philadelphia. While participation in these interviews is not mandatory, applicants who wish to be considered for an AOM interview should submit their CV by July 10, 2026 . Commitment to Fair and Inclusive Employment We believe in creating a workplace that values diversity, promotes equal opportunities, and fosters an inclusive culture where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates, and select faculty solely based on merit and job-related criteria, such as skills, experience, and ability to perform the job. We do not discriminate on the basis of age, ethnicity, gender, religion, marital status, family responsibilities, or disability, and are committed to ensuring a fair and equitable recruitment process for all. We continue to uphold these principles and strive to create a workplace that is welcoming, respectful, and supportive for all. Req ID: 33359 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-in-Psychology/32957-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Psychology Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor in Psychology University-Level Unit: Arts & Social Sciences Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Psychology Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 09/06/2026 National University of Singapore The Department of Psychology at the National University of Singapore (NUS) invites applications for two Assistant Professor positions. With regard to specialty, area is open, although preferences will be given to candidates with expertise in Clinical, Developmental and/or Quantitative Psychology. Candidates should hold a Ph.D. Candidates in Clinical Psychology should also have completed formal graduate-level training as a clinical psychologist. Consistently ranked as one of the top universities in Asia and the world, NUS is internationally respected for its high-quality teaching and research. Within NUS, the Department of Psychology has well-established undergraduate, graduate research and graduate clinical psychology professional training programmes. The department is made up of a diverse group of local and international faculty who are committed to excellence in teaching and research. Information on the department’s faculty, teaching and research programmes can be found at https://fass.nus.edu.sg/psy/ . NUS offers an internationally competitive 12-month salary package along with various benefits. There are also generous start-up packages tailored to the new faculty’s research needs. Beyond University resources, there are substantial opportunities to secure research grants from government agencies and other funding organizations. Interested applicants should submit their complete applications online at https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-in-Psychology/32957-en_GB , comprising the following: CV Research statement: A statement (up to 3 pages) of major accomplishments in research, citing up to 5 significant publications, creative works or other scholarly contributions, and explaining their significance. Teaching statement: A statement (up to 3 pages) of teaching philosophy and methodology. List of all Ph.D. and postdoctoral supervisors or senior authors with close and regular collaborations (full name, institution and email address) Sample copies of significant publications (up to 5) Evidence of teaching ability (e.g. student feedback or peer review reports) and contributions to education (e.g. curriculum development, pedagogical innovation, production of teaching materials), if any Applicants should also arrange for at least 3 letters of reference (including one from the candidate’s main Ph.D. advisor, and one from the candidate’s postdoctoral supervisor) to be sent directly to Ms Loo Bee Bee at psylbb@nus.edu.sg . Review of applications begins 1 November 2026. We regret that only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Campus visits are expected to take place in January 2027. Prior to campus visits, remote pre-interviews with shortlisted candidates may be conducted. Queries may be directed to A/P Stuart Derbyshire, Chair of the Search Committee at stuart.derbyshire@nus.edu.sg . Req ID: 32957 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28ECE%29/33029-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (ECE)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (ECE) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (ECE) University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Electrical and Computer Engineering Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 22/05/2026 Job Description The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) at the National University of Singapore (NUS) is seeking a candidate at the rank of Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) in the area of machine learning and artificial intelligence. The candidate is expected lead active and externally funded research program and collaborative research with colleagues in other disciplines to address challenges that achieve scientific and societal impact are encouraged. Besides research, the candidate is also expected to contribute actively to teaching and service roles at the Department, College, or University level. Interested applicants are invited to submit a detailed CV, a teaching philosophy statement, list of publications, statement of research interests and plans, contact details of at least 3 referees, and the NUS Personal Data Consent for Job Applicants. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for a campus visit and interview. Applications will be accepted until the available position is filled. Qualifications The successful candidate must have an earned doctorate in Electrical Engineering and/or Computer Engineering or an allied field. Candidates must have an established track record in research. Req ID: 33029 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
