    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer-in-Nutrition-and-Lifestyle-Medicine/32801-en_GB": {
      "title": "Outstanding Opportunity: Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Nutrition and Lifestyle Medicine",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Nutrition and Lifestyle Medicine Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Nutrition and Lifestyle Medicine University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean-Med-Global Centre for Asian Women’s Health Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 07/05/2026 Outstanding Opportunity: Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Nutrition and Lifestyle Medicine The National University of Singapore (NUS) Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine invites applications for a Lecturer / Senior Lecturer position for the Master of Science in Nutrition and Lifestyle Medicine programme. Learn more about the programme here: https://medicine.nus.edu.sg/graduatestudies/education/msc-in-nutrition-and-lifestyle-medicine/ This innovative postgraduate programme is at the forefront of advancing evidence-based prevention, precision health, and lifestyle medicine through education, research, and professional training. The programme brings together nutrition science, physical activity, behavioural medicine, sleep health, stress management, and risk reduction to equip future healthcare leaders with the tools to improve health span and reduce chronic disease burden. We seek an outstanding educator who is passionate about transforming healthcare through lifestyle-based approaches and shaping the next generation of practitioners, researchers, and leaders in this rapidly growing field. Position Overview This position offers an exciting opportunity to contribute to the strategic growth and academic excellence of a pioneering Master of Science  programme (MSc) at the NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine. The successful candidate will work closely with programme leadership, faculty, and partners to strengthen teaching, curriculum innovation, student engagement, and research impact. Appointment level will be Lecturer or Senior Lecturer , depending on the candidate’s track record in teaching, leadership, and scholarly achievements. Main Duties and Responsibilities Design, teach, and evaluate modules MSc in Nutrition and Lifestyle Medicine Program  across areas such as nutrition, culinary medicine,  exercise as medicine, obesity management, preventive medicine, behavioural change, sleep, stress, and precision nutrition. Deliver engaging teaching across postgraduate, executive, and continuing professional education formats. Supervise and mentor students in capstone projects, applied learning, and research activities. Support admissions, student engagement, programme promotion, and stakeholder partnerships. Contribute to conferences, workshops, webinars, and outreach initiatives that strengthen programme visibility and impact. Participate actively in interdisciplinary research aligned with nutrition, lifestyle medicine, preventive health, or related areas. Foster collaborations with healthcare institutions, industry, public health bodies, and international academic partners. Applicants Should Have PhD, MD, MBBS, or equivalent doctoral qualification in Medicine, Nutrition, Dietetics, Exercise Science, Public Health, Allied Health, Behavioural Science, or a related discipline. Demonstrated teaching experience in higher education or professional training. Strong interest in preventive health, nutrition, healthy aging, and lifestyle medicine. Experience in curriculum development or programme leadership is advantageous. Proven record of publications, presentations, or professional impact in relevant fields. Experience supervising students or mentoring professionals is desirable. Skills and Attributes Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage diverse learners and stakeholders. Passionate educator who can inspire future leaders in healthcare. Ability to work effectively in interdisciplinary and multicultural environments. Innovative mindset with interest in educational technology and modern learning methods. Organised, proactive, and able to contribute to a fast-growing programme environment. Curious, forward-thinking, and committed to improving population health outcomes Why Join Us This is a unique opportunity to join one of the world’s top universities and contribute to a future-facing programme addressing some of the greatest health challenges of our time through nutrition and lifestyle medicine. Multiple positions are available and will remain open until qualified applicants are found. First round of application review will start on June 1st, 2026. Applicants should email 1) a curriculum vitae; 2) a teaching statement, and a statement of research interests; and 3) name and contact information of three references to the contact as detailed below. Professor Cuilin Zhang Director, MSc. of Nutrition and Lifestyle Medicine Program Director, Global Center for Women’s Health Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine National University of Singapore Email: obgzc@nus.edu.sg  (in the email subject, please clearly state “Application-faculty NLM”) Req ID: 32801 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Department-of-Biochemistry%29/32650-en_GB": {
      "title": "Position Summary",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Department of Biochemistry) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Department of Biochemistry) University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Biochemistry Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 27/04/2026 . Job Title: Assistant Professor Institution: National University of Singapore (NUS) Department/Faculty: Biochemistry, Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Translational Research Program: Healthy Longevity Translational Research Programme (HL TRP) Location: Singapore Appointment Type: Full-time, Tenure-track Position Summary The Department of Biochemistry at the Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine, National University of Singapore (NUS) invites applications for the position of tenure track Assistant Professor. We seek an exceptional and motivated individual to develop and lead an innovative research programme at the interface of computational biology, epigenomics, and aging, with an emphasis on integrating multi-omics approaches and AI/ML-based modelling to advance our understanding of age-associated diseases and healthy longevity. The successful candidate will be expected to: (i) participate in the Healthy Longevity Translational Research Programme, fostering and working within a highly collaborative, interdisciplinary environment spanning computational and experimental biology; (ii) acquire and sustain robust extramural research funding, including nationally competitive grants such as the NRF Fellowship; (iii) teach life sciences, medical, and/or dental education courses to undergraduate and postgraduate students; and (iv) train and mentor graduate students and postdoctoral trainees. Key Responsibilities Establish an independent, externally funded research programme in computational biology, epigenomics, and/or aging with a focus on translational approaches to healthy longevity. Conduct cutting-edge research that contributes to the HL TRP’s goals, including single-cell and spatial multi-omics, epigenomic regulation, brain aging, neurodegenerative disease mechanisms, AI/ML-driven predictive modelling, and biomarker or therapeutic discovery for longevity interventions. Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams including clinicians, scientists, and other stakeholders to drive impactful research. Mentor and supervise undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral researchers. Teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses in areas related to biochemistry, anchored under the Department of Biochemistry. Publish high-quality, peer-reviewed research in leading journals and present findings at national and international conferences. Actively participate in the department events, workshops, and outreach activities. Qualifications Essential: PhD or equivalent doctoral degree in computational biology, bioinformatics, epigenomics, molecular biology, biochemistry, or a related field. At least 3 years of postdoctoral research experience. Proven track record of research excellence as evidenced by first author original high impact publications. Strong potential to secure competitive external funding. Expertise in single-cell or spatial multi-omics, epigenomic analysis, computational genomics, and/or AI/ML approaches applied to biological systems. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary teams. Ready to lead a research group independently. Excellent communication and leadership skills. . Desirable: Experience in teaching and curriculum development at the graduate level. Experience in mentoring and supervising research trainees. Research experience in aging biology, neurodegeneration, transposable element biology, or predictive modelling of disease trajectories. Familiarity with regulatory and ethical requirements for translational research. What We Offer Access to state-of-the-art research facilities and core resources. Opportunities for collaboration with leading researchers. Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package. A supportive environment fostering career development and advancement. Opportunities to engage in impactful, translational research that addresses pressing global health challenges. Application Process Applicants should submit the following: A cover letter outlining their research and teaching interests. A detailed curriculum vitae (CV). A statement of research accomplishments and future plans. A statement of teaching philosophy. At least three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. About Department of Biochemistry The Department of Biochemistry at the NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine is a vibrant research-intensive department with strengths spanning healthy longevity, cancer science, precision medicine, infectious diseases, synthetic biology, metabolic engineering, structural biology, epigenomics, computational biology, and translational medicine. The Department contributes to multiple translational research programmes including the Healthy Longevity, Precision Medicine, Infectious Diseases and Synthetic Biology Translational Research Programmes. Faculty members maintain active collaborations across engineering, computing, and clinical disciplines, and the Department is home to a dynamic community of graduate students and postdoctoral researchers. Situated within Singapore’s thriving biomedical research ecosystem, the Department offers an exceptional environment for interdisciplinary research and innovation at the forefront of the life sciences. About NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine The NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine is Singapore’s oldest and Asia’s top medical school, celebrating its 125th year anniversary in 2025. Today, the school produces cutting edge and impactful research, together with innovative education, seeking to impact change and enhance the practice of medicine in Singapore and beyond. The School is an integral part of a comprehensive university (NUS), with deep collaborative platforms across engineering, computer science, social science, public health, and others, and a long standing joint venture in the National University Health System (NUHS). The NUHS ecosystem is Singapore’s premier Academic Health Centre, encompassing three tertiary hospitals (National University Hospital, Ng Teng Fong Hospital and Alexander Hospital), three national specialist centres (National University Heart Centre, National University Cancer Institute and National University Centre for Oral Health), a primary care system and three health schools (medical school, dental school and school of public health), lending invaluable resource for clinical and translational research, not commonly found elsewhere. Together with other healthcare partners and research institutes in Singapore, the school is an important player in Singapore’s vibrant research and biotech ecosystem. Req ID: 32650 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Lecturer-%28Division-of-Industrial-Design%29/32630-en_GB": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Division of Industrial Design)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Division of Industrial Design) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Lecturer (Division of Industrial Design) University-Level Unit: College of Design and Engineering Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Division of Industrial Design Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 24/04/2026 Job Description •    Conduct lectures and tutorials (discussion groups) and support students via email, office hours. •    Provide administrative support and assist in the day to day running of the module. •    Prepare educational resources and course materials. •    Evaluate module assessment components. •    Assist in curriculum development. Qualifications •    A PhD in a design related discipline, or one close to completion with a strong track record in education or professional engagements and be able to advance the trajectory of the programme. •    Ability to work well independently and as a member of an interdisciplinary team with diverse interests and opinions; team teaching experience preferred. •    Experience with interdisciplinary curriculum design and development preferred. •    Commitment to continual pedagogical improvement and a scholarly approach to education. Req ID: 32630 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Senior-LecturerLecturer-%28Healthy-Longevity%29/32563-en_GB": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (Healthy Longevity)",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (Healthy Longevity) Job Details | National University of Singapore Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (Healthy Longevity) By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Job Alerts Link Apply now Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (Healthy Longevity) University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean-Med-Healthy Longevity Translational Research Programme Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location: Kent Ridge Campus Posted On: 21/04/2026 ▲ Collapse Job Title: Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (Healthy Longevity) University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Dean-Med-Healthy Longevity Translational Research Programme Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 21/04/2026 . The Academy for Healthy Longevity (the Academy) at the Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine, NUS, seeks applications for a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer position. The Academy is leading advancements in Geroscience and Precision Geromedicine through innovative education, research, and its dissemination. The Academy embraces creativity and bold thinking, consistently reimagining education and research to drive better outcomes and lasting impact. By challenging the status quo, and exploring innovative approaches, we inspire transformative learning and research experiences that endure. Position Overview This position offers the opportunity to shape the future of our educational and capacity-building initiatives, working closely with the Academy’s leadership team. The appointment level will be Lecturer or Senior Lecturer, based on the candidate's track record in education leadership, delivery, and research. This is a three-year position, with potential for renewal based on performance. Main duties and responsibilities Contribute to the development and delivery of the new Masters program in Geroscience and Precision Geromedicine. Design, deliver, and evaluate curricula for undergraduate, postgraduate, and continuing professional education, including undergraduates and/or official graduate students, MSc-level courses, short courses, masterclasses, and executive education. Provide academic support for the Academy activities, such as organizing international conferences and workshops. Communicate effectively with a wide range of stakeholders about the Academy’s educational activities and impacts. Participate actively in the research activities of the Academy. The applicant should have: Keen interest in the development of this emerging field. PhD in Medicine, Nursing, Allied Health, Life Sciences, or a related field with relevant teaching experience. Experience in educational approaches and training at the undergraduate/graduate level is preferred. Experience in curriculum design is advantageous. Proven track record of publications and presentations at international or national scientific conferences, particularly in medical and health professions education. Skills and Abilities: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, able to collaborate effectively with an interdisciplinary team. Be a creative educator with inspiring skills for the next generation of leaders in healthcare. Proficiency in educational software and technology. Curiosity catalyser, spark interest and curiosity in students. Req ID: 32563 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Medical-Education-Research-&-Evaluation/32560-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Medical Education Research & Evaluation",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Medical Education Research & Evaluation Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor of Medical Education Research & Evaluation University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Office of Education Employee Category: Others Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 20/04/2026 Job Description Duke-NUS Medical School, a US-style graduate-entry medical school in Singapore, is seeking an innovative and skilled Assistant of Medical Education Research & Evaluation to join the Education Advancement Department. This position plays a central role in advancing the school’s commitment to continuous quality improvement (QI) and to the development of rigorous medical education research that informs educational practice, faculty development, and ultimately patient care. The successful candidate will lead and contribute to theory-informed, methodologically rigorous medical education research, using quantitative, qualitative, and mixed methods, including AI-enabled analytic approaches where appropriate. Responsibilities include developing research questions, study designs, and evaluation frameworks, identifying meaningful performance indicators, and generating evidence to address scholarly questions relevant to medical and health professions education. The role involves close collaboration with programme leaders, educators, and institutional stakeholders to ensure that research and evaluation activities inform decision-making, support innovation, and contribute to generalizable, outcomes-oriented educational scholarship that bridges education, clinical practice, and health systems improvement. Job Role • Lead the design and oversight of systematic evaluation processes for key educational programmes, including defining key performance indicators, developing evaluation frameworks, and analysing data to support programme refinement. • Lead efforts to ensure that programme evaluations are aligned with institutional goals and contribute meaningfully to educational effectiveness. • Partner with the QA lead and other stakeholders to translate evaluation findings into actionable recommendations that drive continuous improvement in educational programmes. • Develop and implement strategies to enhance the quality and outcomes of educational offerings based on data-driven insights. • Serve as a liaison between the Quality Assurance team and other Departments, ensuring that evaluation and research efforts are strategically aligned with institutional objectives. • Facilitate stakeholder consultations and feedback loops to refine and adapt evaluation frameworks, ensuring stakeholder perspectives are incorporated. • Collaborate with internal and external research teams on study design, leading or co-leading research projects, research publications, and identifying opportunities for advancing educational research. • Support stakeholders in interpreting evaluation findings and developing their own improvement plans based on evidence and logical frameworks, fostering a culture of data-informed decision-making. Qualifications • Advanced Degree (MD/MBBS, Ph.D., Ed.D., or equivalent) in education, programme evaluation, educational research, or a related field. • Evidence of scholarly output in a health related field (e.g., peer-reviewed publications). • Strong background in educational research methods, with expertise in programme evaluation methodologies and data analysis. • Proven ability to manage multiple projects and work collaboratively across Departments. • Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to present complex data in a clear, accessible manner to diverse audiences. • Strong collaborative skills, able to support and guide teams to interpret and apply evaluation and research findings for programme improvement. • Experience engaging stakeholders in programme evaluation processes, helping to foster their understanding and involvement in quality improvement initiatives. • Knowledge of evidence-based strategies for educational program enhancement. • Ability to drive collaborative research initiatives and contribute to the scholarship of educational advancement. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Req ID: 32560 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-in-Immunology-Translational-Research-Program-%28ITRP%29/32383-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor in Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Microbiology And Immunology Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 10/04/2026 . Job Title: Assistant Professor in Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) Institution: National University of Singapore (NUS) Department/Faculty: Microbiology and Immunology, Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Translational Research Program: Immunology Location: Singapore Appointment Type: Full-time, Tenure-track Position Summary The Immunology Translational Research Program (IDTRP) at the Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine, National University of Singapore (NUS) invites applications for the position of tenure track Assistant Professor. We seek an exceptional and motivated individual to develop and lead a research program in Immunology, with a focus on translational research that bridges fundamental discoveries and clinical applications. The ideal candidate should have strong expertise and interests in neutrophil biology, particularly in the area of cellular ageing. The successful applicant will join a vibrant and collaborative team dedicated to advancing the understanding, prevention, and treatment of infectious diseases and cancer. . Key Responsibilities Establish an independent, externally funded research program in immunology with an emphasis on translational approaches. Conduct cutting-edge research that contributes to ITRP’s goals, including vaccine development, antimicrobial resistance, pathogen-host interactions, anti-tumor immunity, immune ageing, and public health interventions. Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams including clinicians, scientists, and other stakeholders to drive impactful research. Mentor and supervise undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral researchers. Teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses in areas related to microbiology or immunology, anchored under the Department of Microbiology & Immunology. Publish high-quality, peer-reviewed research in leading journals and present findings at national and international conferences. Actively participate in ITRP’s events, workshops, and outreach activities. . Qualifications Essential: PhD, MD, or equivalent, with at least three years of postdoctoral experience in microbiology, immunology, epidemiology, or a related field. Proven track record of research excellence as evidenced by first author original high impact publications. Strong potential to secure competitive external funding. Expertise in translational research methodologies. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in interdisciplinary teams. Excellent communication and leadership skills. Desirable: Experience in teaching and curriculum development at the graduate level. Experience in mentoring and supervising research trainees. Research experience in neutrophil biology, microbial infection, and sepsis. Familiarity with regulatory and ethical requirements for translational research. . What We Offer Access to state-of-the-art research facilities and core resources. Opportunities for collaboration with leading researchers. Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package. A supportive environment fostering career development and advancement. Opportunities to engage in impactful, translational research that addresses pressing global health challenges. . Application Process Applicants should submit the following: A cover letter outlining their research and teaching interests. A detailed curriculum vitae (CV). A statement of research accomplishments and future plans. A statement of teaching philosophy. At least three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. . About Immunology Translational Research Program The Immunology Translational Research Program (ITRP) at the National University of Singapore (NUS) is driven by a vision to transform medicine through immunological research and a mission to advance collaborative, cutting-edge science that harnesses the immune system to improve human health. Grounded in the belief that a deep understanding of immune mechanisms is essential for preventing, diagnosing, and treating disease, ITRP fosters a highly collaborative and interdisciplinary environment where scientists and clinicians work together to generate impactful discoveries. Looking ahead, ITRP aims to establish itself as a leading centre for immunology in Southeast Asia by strengthening cross-institutional collaboration, partnering with hospitals to bring research from bench to bedside, and attracting and training the next generation of immunologists and clinician-scientists. Through these efforts, the programme strives to deliver meaningful advances that benefit patients and public health across the region. About Department of Microbiology and Immunology The Department of Microbiology and Immunology has distinguished itself in biomedical research and has a broad spectrum of expertise. Research in the Department encompasses very diverse questions and uses a wide variety of approaches, experimental systems, and techniques. Principal Investigators of the Department are internationally recognized for research on immunology, medical virology, bacteriology, parasitology, molecular biology and biotechnology. . About NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine The NUS Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine is Singapore’s oldest and Asia’s top medical school, celebrating its 125th year anniversary in 2025. Today, the school produces cutting edge and impactful research, together with innovative education, seeking to impact change and enhance the practice of medicine in Singapore and beyond. The School is an integral part of a comprehensive university (NUS), with deep collaborative platforms across engineering, computer science, social science, public health, and others, and a long standing joint venture in the National University Health System (NUHS). The NUHS ecosystem is Singapore’s premier Academic Health Centre, encompassing three tertiary hospitals (National University Hospital, Ng Teng Fong Hospital and Alexander Hospital), three national specialist centres (National University Heart Centre, National University Cancer Institute and National University Centre for Oral Health), a primary care system and three health schools (medical school, dental school and school of public health), lending invaluable resource for clinical and translational research, not commonly found elsewhere. Together with other healthcare partners and research institutes in Singapore, the school is an important player in Singapore’s vibrant research and biotech ecosystem. Req ID: 32383 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-%28Tenure-Track%29%2C-CSCB/32034-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor (Tenure Track), CSCB",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor (Tenure Track), CSCB Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant / Associate / Full Professor (Tenure Track), CSCB University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Office of Research Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 10/03/2026 Job Description Duke-NUS Medical School (Duke-NUS), Singapore’s only graduate-entry medical school, is a landmark collaboration between two world-ranking institutions of higher education – Duke University and the National University of Singapore (NUS). Duke-NUS provides innovative education and impactful research to advance medicine and improve lives. Through our strategic partnership with Singapore Health Services (SingHealth), the largest public healthcare cluster in Singapore, the SingHealth/Duke-NUS Academic Medical Centre fosters cutting-edge collaborations in translational and clinical research, driving discoveries and solutions to global healthcare challenges. The Programme in Cancer & Stem Cell Biology (CSCB) is one of the Signature Research Programmes in Duke-NUS. The Programme is dedicated to advancing deep biological understanding of cancer and stem cell systems, spanning molecular, cellular, tissue, and organismal levels. We value research that challenges existing paradigms, uncovers new principles of disease biology, and lays the foundation for future translational and clinical advances. More information about CSCB faculty, research activities and facilities can be found at www.duke-nus.edu.sg/cscb . CSCB is seeking outstanding scientists who are driven by fundamental discoveries, interdisciplinary research, and intellectual curiosity, and who aspire to see their research ultimately inform better improved cancer prevention, diagnosis, and treatment, while advancing as well as driving the frontiers of novel drug development. The successful applicant should be highly collaborative and demonstrates strong enthusiasm to actively engage with both basic scientists and clinicians across disciplines. They will be expected to address complex research questions and compelling healthcare concerns, work within multidisciplinary teams to advance the frontiers of science, and contribute meaningfully to the School’s and the nation’s key priority areas. Job Requirements Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree with a strong background and proven track record across the full spectrum of cancer and stem cell biology. Areas of expertise may include, but are not limited to, RNA biology, therapeutics discovery, cancer immunology, functional genomics, computational and systems biology, cancer as an age-related disease, and emerging technologies. Excellence in any area of basic or discovery-driven cancer and stem cell research will be strongly considered. Research independence and demonstrated leadership in managing a productive research team. Exceptional track record in securing competitive research funding and publications in high impact scientific journals. Prior experience in translating research towards pre-clinical or commercial applications is desirable but not essential. Ability to mentor and train graduate students and postdoctoral research staff. Interested candidates should send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, and the names of three referees in support of their application via email at hr@duke-nus.edu.sg and attention it to: Administrative Chair Search Committee, CSCB Duke-NUS Medical School Applications will be open until the position is filled and we anticipate beginning interviewing candidates from June 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. More Information Location: Outram Campus Organization: Duke-NUS Medical School Department : Office of Research Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 32034 Req ID: 32034 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Cancer-Science-Institute%29/28463-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Cancer Science Institute) University-Level Unit: Cancer Science Institute of Singapore Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Administration Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 05/03/2026 Job Description The Cancer Science Institute of Singapore (CSI) is seeking outstanding and visionary researchers for multiple faculty positions, ranging from Assistant to Full Professor . As a globally recognized leader with a reputation of excellence in cancer biology, immunology, and translational medicine, CSI is dedicated to transforming cancer detection, treatment, and prevention to improve patient outcomes. Our institute is purpose-built for cancer research and integrates cutting-edge technology, multidisciplinary approaches, and strong clinical collaborations to achieve groundbreaking discoveries. Our work spans the biological, computational, and engineering sciences, with a mission to address the unique cancer landscape of Asia while contributing to global progress. We are expanding our faculty to complement existing strengths and seed new, strategic directions in cancer research. We invite applications from exceptional scientists working in any area of cancer research, with particular interest in the following fields: Computational Biology of Cancer Evolution Cancer Immunology and Immunotherapy Epithelial Cancer Biology Successful candidates will join a dynamic, collaborative environment and gain access to: State-of-the-art laboratories and world-class core facilities Generous start-up support and institutional research funding A competitive salary package aligned with global benchmarks Opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaborations within NUS and with global academic and industry partners Candidates should possess and demonstrate the following: A PhD and/or M.D. degree in a relevant discipline An established record of research excellence, with international competitiveness for their career stage A distinguished track record of research, publications, and leadership in cancer research Proven ability to secure funding and drive impactful, multidisciplinary research programs Application Documents To facilitate the application process, Candidates are invited to submit the following: Cover Letter Describe your background, expertise, and alignment with CSI's mission Comprehensive CV Include a full publication list, grants, awards, and leadership roles Key Achievements and Future Plans (up to 1500 words) Summarize your pivotal contributions to cancer research Outline your future research goals and potential synergies with CSI References Contact details of three senior colleagues willing to provide letters of reference Req ID: 28463 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/AssistantAssociate-Professor-in-AI-for-Medical-Education/31785-en_GB": {
      "title": "Scope of Position",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in AI for Medical Education Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in AI for Medical Education University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Office of Education Employee Category: Others Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 13/02/2026 Scope of Position Duke-NUS Medical School invites applications for a full-time Assistant/Associate Professor in AI for Medical Education within the Office of Education. This innovative role will apply Artificial Intelligence technologies and approaches to support and enhance educational delivery, assessment, and learning experiences, while also contributing to curriculum development that prepares future physicians to practice effectively in an AI-enhanced healthcare environment. Working in close partnership with MD curriculum leadership, teams, faculty, administrators, and students, the successful applicant will co-lead and support initiatives to develop and integrate AI-powered educational tools across our MD curriculum, conduct research on AI applications in medical education, and design and deliver an AI literacy curriculum. This position represents a unique opportunity to shape the future of medical education at the intersection of technology and healthcare. The successful applicant will be eligible for faculty appointment at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level at Duke-NUS; rank will be commensurate with experience, achievement and recognition. The postholder will collaborate with clinician educators and scientists across all health professions and disciplines in the SingHealth Duke-NUS Academic Medical Centre. Roles and Responsibilities Roles and Responsibilities: - Partner with curriculum teams to design, implement, and evaluate AI-powered educational tools such as intelligent tutoring systems, adaptive learning platforms, virtual patient simulations, etc - Develop AI applications for personalized learning experiences that respond to individual student needs and learning patterns - Support the development and deployment of AI-driven assessment systems that provide automated feedback, performance analytics, and competency evaluation - Conduct original research on the effectiveness of AI applications in medical education - Publish findings in peer-reviewed journals and present at national and international conferences - Secure internal and external funding to support AI-driven educational innovation projects - Collaborate with Education and IT teams to support learning analytics and educational data management throughout the School - Contribute to the development and delivery of AI literacy curriculum for medical students - Conduct workshops and training sessions for faculty on both using AI tools and teaching about AI - Mentor students, health care educators and investigators interested in Artificial Intelligence for medical education - Participate in the general teaching, service and administrative responsibilities of the Office of Education as determined by their Reporting Officer - Develop strong working relationships with collaborators both within Duke-NUS and the wider SingHealth Duke-NUS Academic Medical Centre - Appropriate duties as assigned by reporting officer Qualifications Education: - Doctoral degree in Computer Science, Biomedical Informatics, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Educational Technology, or closely related field - Postdoctoral training or previous faculty appointment in Artificial Intelligence, Medical Education, Educational Technology or other relevant area is desirable but not essential Technical Expertise: - Demonstrated expertise in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning methods and their practical application - Strong programming skills (Python, R, or similar languages) used in AI and data science development - Experience developing, training, and deploying AI/ML models using modern frameworks and tools. - Knowledge of relevant AI domains such as Natural Language Processing, Computer Vision, and/or multimodal learning - Familiarity with learning analytics, data management and educational/healthcare data environments - Understanding of learning management systems or digital learning platforms is advantageous Experience - Minimum 3 years of experience in the development and practical use of AI/ML applications in educational contexts, healthcare settings or other relevant domains - Experience with learning analytics and educational data mining - Experience with human-centred design and user experience research - Demonstrable commitment to research and scholarship. For example, research productivity, preferably in a higher education institute, healthcare organization or medical education setting; grant funded research as Principal Investigator or lead; peer reviewed research publications; visiting appointments; advisory roles; consultancy; other evidence of scholarly activities; knowledge creation, synthesis, application and dissemination Competencies: - Knowledge of ethical considerations in AI, including bias, fairness, and privacy - Exceptional time management, organizational skills and the ability to work on multiple projects simultaneously and meet project deadlines - Accessible, calm, flexible, and mature individual with superlative interpersonal skills that permit him/her to work independently as well as in a team environment, to establish credibility with staff at all levels and of different disciplines and backgrounds, and to be persuasive in both one-to-one and group settings - Commitment to maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion in sharing of information. - Excellent written and verbal communication and presentation skills with ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences - Ability to translate Artificial Intelligence / Machine Learning techniques and Data Analytics approaches to medical education and practice - Ability to mentor students and faculty in scholarship within the domain of Artificial Intelligence for medical education More Information All applications including a letter of interest and a curriculum vitae should be submitted online. Informal enquiries are welcome and should be directed to Prof Fernando Bello (f.bello@duke-nus.edu.sg). We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified Req ID: 31785 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant%2C-Associate%2C-Full-Professor-%28Tenure-Track%29%2C-CVMD-Programme/28864-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, Full Professor (Tenure Track), CVMD Programme",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, Full Professor (Tenure Track), CVMD Programme Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant, Associate, Full Professor (Tenure Track), CVMD Programme University-Level Unit: Duke-NUS Medical School Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Office of Research Employee Category: Tenurable Faculty Location_ONB: Outram Campus Posting Start Date: 29/01/2026 Job Description Duke-NUS Medical School (Duke-NUS), Singapore’s only graduate-entry medical school, was established as a landmark collaboration between two world-ranking institutions of higher education – Duke University and National University of Singapore. Duke-NUS provides innovative education and impactful research to enhance the practice of medicine in Singapore and beyond. The School also has strong research ties with Singapore Health Services (SingHealth), one of Singapore’s major healthcare providers, other major research institutions in Singapore, and with Duke University The Programme in Cardiovascular and Metabolic Disorders (CVMD) is one of the Signature Research Programmes in Duke-NUS. The overarching aim of the Programme is to define the molecular mechanisms underlying human health and disease and to discover new approaches to prevent, diagnose and treat cardio-metabolic illnesses. More information about CVMD faculty, research activities and facilities can be found at www.duke-nus.edu.sg/cvmd/ . Job Requirements Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent degree with a strong background and proven track record in cellular and systemic metabolism, metabolomics/lipidomics, renal and cardiovascular biology and medicine, and integrative data sciences, including systems genetics and related fields. Research independence and demonstrated leadership in managing a productive research team. Exceptional track record in securing competitive research funding and publications in high impact scientific journals. Prior experience in translating research towards pre-clinical or commercial applications is desirable but not essential. Ability to mentor and train graduate students and postdoctoral research staff Interested candidates should send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a summary of research accomplishments and outline of research plans or programs, as well as arrange to have three (3) letters of reference sent in support of their application via email at hr@duke-nus.edu.sg and attention it to: Administrative Chair Search Committee, CVMD Duke-NUS Medical School Applications will be open until the position is filled. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. More Information Location: Outram Campus Organization: Duke-NUS Medical School Department : Office of Research Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 28864 Req ID: 28864 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://careers.nus.edu.sg/job/Assistant-Professor-%28Alice-Lee-Center-for-Nursing-Studies%29/22128-en_GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Alice Lee Center for Nursing Studies)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Alice Lee Center for Nursing Studies) Job Details | National University of Singapore By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Sign In / Create Account HOME ALL JOBS ACADEMIC POSITIONS RESEARCH & OTHER TEACHING POSITIONS EXECUTIVE & ADMINISTRATIVE POSITIONS Job Description Apply now ▲ Collapse Job Title: Assistant Professor (Alice Lee Center for Nursing Studies) University-Level Unit: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Faculty/Department-Level Unit: Alice Lee Centre for Nursing Studies Employee Category: Other Teaching Staff Location_ONB: Kent Ridge Campus Posting Start Date: 02/05/2024 Job Description Assistant Professor (Practice Track) The Alice Lee Centre for Nursing Studies (NUS Nursing) invites interested applicants who are Advanced Practice Nurses to apply for the position of Assistant Professor (Practice Track). Assistant Professors on the Practice Track should contribute towards the educational mission of the University through teaching, in addition to their contributions in their nursing practice. Qualifications The successful candidate must have a Bachelor Degree in Nursing and a Master of Nursing (MN) qualification. They must have at least 3 years of relevant practice experience as an APN. Terms of Appointment This is a non-tenurable track and the candidate will be appointed on a first contract of up to three years, with renewal contract(s) of up to five years in total, subject to performance of the faculty member and needs of the hiring unit. They will have to apply and get promoted to Associate Professor (Practice) within a period of eight years. Application Dossier: Interested applicants are invited to submit a CV to nurleee@nus.edu.sg Shortlisted candidates will be invited for a campus visit and interview. More Information Location: Kent Ridge Campus Organization: Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine Department : Alice Lee Centre for Nursing Studies Employee Referral Eligible: No Job requisition ID : 22128 Req ID: 22128 Apply now Legal Branding guidelines Contact us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © National University of Singapore. All Rights Reserved."
    }
